hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5401","528 - Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him: one of 'Aqabah, Badr, and Uhud, a naqib. 5395 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of the Muslims who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-'Aqabah among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' ibn 'Amr, and he is a naqib, and he was present at Badr."""
"5402","5396 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' ibn Abi Zuhayr ibn Malik ibn Imri' al-Qays ibn Tha'labah ibn Ka'b ibn al-Khazraj ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj."""
"5403","5397 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Sa'd ibn al-Rabi', and he is a naqib."""
"5404","5398 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'."""
"5405","5399 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those martyred at Uhud with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the Ansar: Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'."""
"5406","5400 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those martyred on the day of Uhud among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'."""
"5407","5401 - Narrated to us Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, my father narrated to me, Isma'il ibn Qays narrated to us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Umm Sa'd, daughter of Sa'd ibn al-Rabi', that she entered upon Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, and he cast his garment for her until she sat upon it, then 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, entered upon him and said: ""O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, who is this?"" He said: This is the daughter of one who is better than me and than you. He said: ""And who is better than me and than you except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"" Abu Bakr said: ""A man who passed away in the lifetime of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having taken his seat in Paradise, while I and you remain."""
"5408","5402 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Ma'bad ibn Ka'b ibn Malik narrated to me, from his brother 'Ubayd Allah ibn Ka'b, from his father Ka'b ibn Malik, who said: We went out in the Hajj in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, and the naqib of Banu al-Khazraj was 'Abd Allah ibn Rawahah, and Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'."
"5409","5403 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Humayd al-Tawil, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf came to Madinah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between him and Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' al-Ansari, so Sa'd offered him to share his family and wealth equally, and he had two wives, so 'Abd al-Rahman said to him: May Allah bless you in your family and wealth; show me the way to the market. He said: So he went to the market and profited some dried yogurt and some clarified butter, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him after some days with a trace of yellow perfume upon him and said: ""What is this, 'Abd al-Rahman?"" He said: I have married a woman of the Ansar. He said: ""What did you give her as dowry?"" He said: The weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"5410","5404 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah, narrated to us Sa'id ibn 'Ufayr, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Bilal, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Quraysh and the Ansar, so he made brotherhood between Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, so Sa'd said to him: I have wealth, so it is between me and you in two halves, and I have two wives, so see which of them is more beloved to you and I will divorce her, and when she becomes lawful then marry her. He said: May Allah bless you in your family and wealth; show me the way to the market. And he did not return until he returned with dates and dried yogurt, then he had surplus, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw upon him a trace of yellow perfume and said: ""What is this?"" So I said: I have married a woman of the Ansar. He said: ""What did you give her as dowry?"" He said: The weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"5411","5405 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik: that when Ibn 'Awf came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he entrusted him to Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' and said: This is your brother. So he took him home, gave him supper, and spread a bed for him. When morning came, Sa'd went to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf and greeted him and said: I have the finest two wives among the Ansar and the best two orchards among the Ansar, so look at my two wives and whichever of them pleases you more, I will divorce her for you, for her family will not disobey me, and look at whichever of my two orchards you wish and take it. But he accepted nothing from him."
"5412","5406 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us 'Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Sa'd and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, so he took him back to his family and said: Choose whichever of my two wives you wish and I will divorce her for you, and my wealth is halves for you. So 'Abd al-Rahman said: May Allah bless you in your family and wealth; show me the way to the market. So they showed him to it, and he did not return until he had gained something, then he married a woman of the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone of gold, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him with a trace of yellow perfume upon him and said: ""What is this?"" He said: I have married a woman of the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone of gold. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"5413","5407 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us 'Umarah ibn Zadhan, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, may Allah have mercy on him, emigrated to Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between him and Sa'd, and Sa'd had two orchards and two wives, so Sa'd said to 'Abd al-Rahman: Choose whichever of my two wives you wish and I will leave her for you, and choose whichever of my two orchards you wish. He said: I have no need of your wife nor of your orchard; it is not for this that I accepted Islam, but show me the way to the market. So he showed him, while he had nothing, and he would buy fat, dried yogurt, skins, and other goods, and sell them, until he gathered something, then he married, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a trace of yellow perfume upon him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""'Abd al-Rahman, what is this?"" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have married for a date-stone of gold. He said: Then give a wedding feast, even with a sheep. So he prospered and his wealth grew. Then while 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, was in her house, she heard a sound by which Madinah shook, so she said: What is this? They said: A caravan of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf has come from Sham, and it was seven hundred camels. So 'A'ishah said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I saw 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf entering Paradise crawling. That reached 'Abd al-Rahman, may Allah be pleased with him, so he came to her and asked her about the hadith that had reached him, and she narrated it to him. He said: ""Then I call you to witness that it, with its loads, saddles, and saddlecloths, is in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."""
"5414","529 - Sa'd ibn Mas'ud al-Ansari, ""he used to reside in Madinah."" 5408 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sulayman, narrated to us 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam, from Isma'il, from Qays, who said: We entered upon Sa'd ibn Mas'ud visiting him in illness, and he said: I do not know what they say, but would that what is in this chest of mine were embers. When he died, they looked, and there were in it a thousand or two thousand."
"5415","5409 - Narrated to us 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, and Zakariyya al-Saji, both saying: Narrated to us 'Uqbah ibn Sinan al-Dharra', narrated to us 'Uthman ibn 'Uthman al-Ghatafani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Al-Harith al-Ghatafani came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, share the dates of Madinah with us. He said: ""Until I consult the Sa'ds."" So he sent for Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, Sa'd ibn al-Rabi', Sa'd ibn Khaythamah, and Sa'd ibn Mas'ud, may Allah have mercy on them, and said: ""I know that the Arabs have aimed at you with a single bow, and that al-Harith asks you to share the dates of Madinah with him; if you wish, give him this year of yours, until you consider your affair thereafter."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, is it revelation from heaven, so submission to the command of Allah, or is it from your opinion or desire, so our opinion follows your desire and opinion? If you only intend to preserve us, then by Allah, you have seen us and them on equal terms; they would not obtain a single date from us except by purchase or hospitality. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is what you hear them saying. They said: You have betrayed, O Muhammad. So Hassan ibn Thabit, may Allah have mercy on him, said: al-Sakhbar."
"5416","530 - Sa'd ibn Khaythamah al-Ansari: one of 'Aqabah and Badr. 5410 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""Among those of the Ansar who were present at al-'Aqabah, then among Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf: Sa'd ibn Khaythamah, and he is a naqib."""
"5417","5411 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu 'Amr ibn al-Salam ibn Malik ibn al-Aws: Sa'd ibn Khaythamah."""
"5418","5412 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf: Sa'd ibn Khaythamah."""
"5419","5413 - Narrated to us Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani, narrated to us Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: ""Among those martyred on the day of Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the Ansar: Sa'd ibn Khaythamah."""
"5420","5414 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari, narrated to us Shabab al-'Usfuri, narrated to us Bakr ibn Sulayman, from Ibn Ishaq, and Wahb ibn Jarir, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed at Quba with Kulthum ibn Hidm, brother of Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, and it is said: rather he stayed with Sa'd ibn Khaythamah. He remained among Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, and founded their mosque, and left Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, and Friday overtook him among Banu Salim ibn 'Awf, so he prayed Friday in the mosque in the valley bottom. Ibn Ishaq said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with Abu Ayyub, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the building of his mosque in that year."
"5421","5415 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, among Banu Ghanm ibn al-Silm ibn Malik ibn al-Aws ibn Jariyah: Sa'd ibn Khaythamah."""
"5422","5416 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Hawari al-Wasiti, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Daqiqi, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Muhammad, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Khaythamah, my father narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw as if mercy fell between Banu Salim and Banu Bayadah. So they said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), shall we move to its place? He said: ""No, but bury your dead in it."" So they buried their dead in it."
"5423","5417 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi, narrated to us 'Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi, narrated to us Ziyad ibn 'Abd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among al-Aws: Sa'd ibn Khaythamah ibn al-Harith ibn Malik ibn Ka'b ibn al-Nahhat ibn Ka'b ibn Harithah ibn Ghanm ibn al-Silm ibn Imri' al-Qays ibn Malik ibn al-Aws."""
"5424","5418 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr, narrated to us Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Ma'bad ibn Ka'b ibn Malik narrated to me, from his brother 'Ubayd Allah ibn Ka'b, from his father Ka'b ibn Malik, who said: We went out in the Hajj in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the naqib of Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf was Sa'd ibn Khaythamah."
"5425","5419 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sinan, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Khaythamah, my father narrated to us, from his father, who said: I stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gone. Then I entered an orchard and saw a trellis sprinkled with water, and I saw my wife, so I said: This is not fairness; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is in the scorching heat, while I am in shade and comfort. So I rose to a watering camel and packed it, and to some dates and took them as provision, then my wife called out: Where to, O Abu Khaythamah? So I went out seeking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until when I was partway, 'Umayr ibn Wahb al-Jumahi caught up with me, so I said: You are a bold man, and I know where the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is, and I am a sinful man, so stay behind me until I am alone with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So 'Umayr stayed behind me. When I came in sight of the camp and the people saw me, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be Abu Khaythamah. So I came and said: I nearly perished, O Messenger of Allah. Then I told him my story, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke good to me and supplicated for me."
"5426","531 - Sa'd ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi; he has companionship. 5420 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us Sufyan, from Abu Husayn, from 'Abd Allah ibn Sinan, from Sa'd ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi, who said: Nuh was only named a grateful servant because when he ate and drank he praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"5427","532 - Sa'd ibn 'Umarah, and it is said: 'Umarah ibn Sa'd, Abu Sa'id al-Zuraqi al-Ansari. 5421 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Abu al-Fayd, from 'Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Abu Sa'id, that a man of Ashja' asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My wife is nursing, and I dislike that she become pregnant; shall I practice coitus interruptus with her? He said: What is decreed in the womb will be."
"5428","533 - Sa'd ibn Zayd al-Ashhali; of Badr. 5422 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu 'Abd ibn Ka'b ibn 'Abd al-Ashhal: Sa'd ibn Zayd ibn Malik ibn 'Abd ibn Ka'b."""
"5429","5423 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal: Sa'd ibn Zayd."""
"5430","5424 - Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Ja'far al-Ansari, a man of us called Sulayman ibn Mahmud, of the descendants of Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari, narrated to me, from Sa'd ibn Zayd al-Ashhali, that he gave as a gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a sword from Najran, or a sword from Najran was given as a gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he came to him he gave it to Muhammad ibn Maslamah and said: Strive with this in the path of Allah, and when the necks of people differ, strike the stone with it, then enter your house and be a cast-off mat, until a mistaken hand kills you, or a decreed death comes to you."
"5431","5425 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Habibah, from Zayd ibn Sa'd, from his father: that when his own death was announced to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he came out wrapped in worn garments until he sat upon the pulpit. The people heard of him, and the people of the market attended the mosque. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, preserve my memory regarding this clan of the Ansar, for they are my inner store in which I eat and my repository; accept from their doers of good and overlook their doers of evil."
"5432","534 - Sa'd ibn Malik ibn Sinan ibn Tha'labah, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri; he used to reside in Madinah. 5426 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, who said: ""Salamah ibn al-Akwa', kunya Abu Iyas, and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri died in the year seventy-four."""
"5433","5427 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr saying: ""Abu Sa'id al-Khudri died in the year seventy-four."""
"5434","5428 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban, narrated to us Sulaym ibn Muslim, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Harun, who said: I saw the beard of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri white in locks."
"5435","5429 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, my father narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Rafi', who said: I saw Abu Sa'id al-Khudri dyeing with yellow."
"5436","5430 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to me, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali narrated to us, my mother Umm Sa'id, daughter of Mas'ud ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri - and he is Sa'd ibn Malik ibn Sinan - narrated to me, that she heard Umm 'Abd al-Rahman, daughter of Abu Sa'id, narrating from her father, that he said: The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wounded on the day of Uhud, and Malik ibn Sinan received him and sucked the wound of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever loves to look at one whose blood has mixed with my blood, let him look at Malik ibn Sinan."
"5437","5431 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr saying: ""Abu Sa'id al-Khudri is Sa'd ibn Malik ibn Sinan."""
"5438","5432 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Ishaq ibn Wahb al-'Allaf, narrated to us Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from Abu Harun al-'Abdi, who said: I saw Abu Sa'id al-Khudri with his beard plucked out, so I said: Do you play with your beard? He said: ""No; this is what I met from the oppressors of the people of Sham. They entered upon me in the days of al-Harrah and took what was in the house of goods or firewood, then another party entered upon me and found nothing in the house, so they were aggrieved to leave with nothing."" He said: ""Lay the shaykh down. So they laid me down, and each one of them took a lock of my beard."""
"5439","And what Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, transmitted as musnad. 5433 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib informed me, that 'Amir ibn Yahya informed him, from Hanash al-San'ani, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: There will emerge from this ummah people who pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the target."
"5440","5434 - Narrated to us 'Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri, narrated to us Abu Salih al-Harrani, narrated to us Ibn Lahi'ah, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, that Jamil ibn Abi al-Mada informed him, from his father, who said: Marwan ibn al-Hakam said to Zayd ibn Thabit: How do you eat? He said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you tastes food, let him not wipe his hand until he licks his fingers, for he does not know in which part of his food blessing lies."
"5441","5435 - Narrated to us al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Salih, Nafi' ibn Yazid narrated to me, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever spends the night with the smell of grease on his hand and is afflicted with vitiligo, let him blame none but himself."
"5442","5436 - Narrated to us 'Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri, narrated to us Abu Salih al-Harrani, narrated to us Ibn Lahi'ah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is praying, let him not raise his sight to the sky, lest it be snatched away."
"5443","5437 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi, narrated to us Haywah ibn Shurayh, narrated to us Baqiyyah, from Mubashshir ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of 'Abd al-Muttalib; I am the most eloquent of the Arabs; Quraysh bore me and I grew up among Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr, so whence would faulty speech come to me?"
"5444","5438 - Narrated to us Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba', narrated to us Ibn Abi Fudayk, from al-Dahhak ibn 'Uthman, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no man look at the private parts of a man, nor let a woman look at the private parts of a woman, nor let a man lie with a man, nor a woman with a woman."
"5445","5439 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu Qaza'ah informed me that Abu Nadrah informed him that Abu Sa'id informed him: that the delegation of 'Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make us ransom for you, what beverages are lawful for us? He said: Do not drink in gourds hollowed in the middle. They said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make us ransom for you, do you know what al-naqir is? He said: ""Yes, a trunk hollowed in its middle; nor in pumpkins, nor in green jars, and stick to waterskins tied at the mouth."
"5446","5440 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Zayd, narrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Hakam, narrated to us Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a man is confused in his prayer and does not know whether he added or omitted, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"5447","5441 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Zayd, from 'Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: It was forbidden for a man to drink while standing, and to put his mouth to the mouth of the waterskin and drink from it."
"5448","5442 - Narrated to us al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-'Ayshi, narrated to us Suwayd Abu Hatim, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: We were sitting at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) discussing, this one citing a verse and this one citing a verse, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us as if pomegranate seeds had burst upon his face, and said: ""O you people, is it with this that you were sent? Or with this were you commanded? Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"5449","5443 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Bukayr ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Suwayd al-Sa'idi, that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel led me in prayer: he prayed Zuhr when the sun declined, and prayed 'Asr when the shadow was a stature, and prayed Maghrib when the sun set, and prayed 'Isha when the twilight disappeared, and prayed Fajr when dawn rose. Then he led me on the second day: he prayed Zuhr when the shade of everything was its like, and prayed 'Asr when the shade was two statures, and prayed Maghrib at the hour the sun set, and prayed 'Isha until the first third of the night, and prayed Fajr when the sun was about to rise. Then he said: ""Prayer is between these two times."""
"5450","5444 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah, and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, both saying: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, 'Abd Allah ibn Qurayt narrated to me, that 'Ata ibn Yasar narrated to him that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The five prayers are expiations for what is between them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell me, if a man had a workplace, and between his house and his workplace were five rivers, and when he went to his workplace he worked as Allah willed, and dirt or sweat befell him, then every time he passed a river he bathed, would that not cleanse him of his filth? So likewise the prayers: every time he commits a sin or what Allah wills, then prays a prayer seeking forgiveness, he is forgiven what came before it."
"5451","5445 - Narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Qurayt, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting Ramadan to Ramadan is expiation for what is between them."
"5452","5446 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us 'Amr ibn 'Awn al-Wasiti, narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Abu al-Zinad and Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from Abu Sa'id, that a cripple, mentioning a chronic ailment of his, was by the wall of Umm Sa'd, and a woman appeared pregnant, so she was asked and said: It is from him. So he was asked and confessed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that he be flogged with stalk clusters of date-palm fronds."
"5453","5447 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn al-'Abbas, and 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Raziyan, both saying: Narrated to us 'Abd al-Mu'min ibn 'Ali, narrated to us 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, salt for salt, like for like; whoever increases or seeks increase has dealt in usury. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), your date keeper buys a sa' for two sa's. So he sent for him and said: O Messenger of Allah, my dates are such-and-such, and they will not take them unless I give them extra. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not do so."""
"5454","535 - Sa'd ibn 'A'idh al-Qaraz, the mu'adhdhin, al-Ansari. 5448 - Narrated to us Bishr ibn Musa, narrated to us al-Humaydi, (Ha) and narrated to us Ishaq ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati, narrated to us Hisham ibn 'Ammar, both saying: Narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Ammar ibn Sa'd al-Qaraz, mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my father narrated to me, from my grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal to put his fingers in his ears, and said: It raises your voice. And the adhan of Bilal was in pairs, and his tashahhud doubled, and his iqamah single, with: Qad qamat al-salah, once. And that he used to call the adhan on Friday for Jumu'ah in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the shade was like a sandal strap. And that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went out to the two Eids, would pass by the house of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, then by the people of the tents, then begin with prayer before the sermon, then say takbir seven times in the first before recitation, and five in the last before recitation, then address the people, then leave by the other road, by the road of Banu Zurayq, and slaughter his sacrifice at the edge of the lane with his hand with a knife, then pass by the house of 'Ammar ibn Yasir and the house of Abu Hurayrah at al-Balat. And he would go out to the two Eids walking and return walking, and would say takbir between the parts of the sermon, and say much takbir in the sermon of the two Eids. And when he addressed in war he addressed leaning on a bow, and when he addressed on Friday he addressed leaning on a staff. And Bilal, when he said takbir in the adhan, would face the qiblah, then say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, twice; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, twice, facing the qiblah, then turn to the right of the qiblah and say: Come to prayer, twice, then turn to the left of the qiblah and say: Come to success, twice, then face the qiblah and say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest."
"5455","5449 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Ma'mari, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Musaffa, narrated to us Baqiyyah, narrated to us al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Hafs ibn 'Umar ibn Sa'd al-Qaraz, that his father and his uncles informed him: that Sa'd al-Qaraz was a mu'adhdhin for the people of Quba, then 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, transferred him and took him as mu'adhdhin. The Sunnah in the prayer of Adha and Fitr is for the imam to say seven takbirs in the first before recitation, and five takbirs in the second rak'ah before recitation."
"5456","5450 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Humayd, narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ammar ibn Sa'd, from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, and from 'Ammar and 'Umar, sons of Hafs ibn 'Umar ibn Sa'd, from their fathers, from their grandfathers, from Sa'd, that the first beginning of the adhan was that a man of the Ansar saw it in a dream and informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal to call the adhan, and the Ansari cast it upon him: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; then he repeated: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; Come to prayer, come to prayer; Come to success, come to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah."
"5457","5451 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Awwal, narrated to us Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Ju'fi, al-Hawdi, a shaykh of the people of Madinah, narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had assigned an adhan to him."
"5458","5452 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn Sa'id, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Humayd, narrated to us 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ammar ibn Sa'd ibn 'A'idh al-Qaraz, from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ammar ibn Sa'd, and from 'Ammar and 'Umar, sons of Hafs ibn 'Umar ibn Sa'd, from their fathers, from their grandfathers, from Sa'd al-Qaraz: that whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Quba, Bilal would call the adhan so that the people would know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had come and gather to him. One day he came without Bilal with him, and the black guards looked at one another, so Sa'd climbed a date-stalk for the adhan. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prompted you to call the adhan, O Sa'd? He said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, I saw you among few people, and I did not see Bilal with you, and I saw these blacks looking at one another and at you, so I feared for you from them, and called the adhan. He said: ""You did right, O Sa'd; when you do not see Bilal with me, then call the adhan."" So Sa'd called the adhan three times in the lifetime of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5459","5453 - And with its isnad: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine the two prayers, Maghrib and 'Isha, in rain."
"5460","5454 - And with its isnad: that al-Najashi sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three small spears; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept one for himself, gave 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, one, and 'Umar one. And Bilal would walk with it before him and plant it before him at the two Eids, and he would pray toward it."
"5461","536 - Sa'd ibn Dumayrah al-Sulami, ""he used to reside in Madinah."" 5455 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, Ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, that he heard Ziyad ibn Sa'd ibn Dumayrah al-Sulami narrating from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, that Muhallim ibn Jaththamah al-Laythi killed a man of Ashja' in Islam, and that was the first blood-money case ruled upon by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: 'Uyaynah ibn Badr spoke concerning the killing of the Ashja'i because he is a man of Ghatafan, and al-Aqra' ibn Habis spoke on behalf of Muhallim ibn Jaththamah because he is a man of Khindif. He said: Voices rose, and dispute and clamor increased. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Will you not accept the blood-money, O 'Uyaynah?"" He said: No, by Allah, until I bring upon his women of war and grief the like of what he brought upon my women. He said it twice or thrice, until a man of Banu Layth called Mukaytil stood up, with a shield in his hand, and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I find no likeness for what he did at the beginning of Islam but sheep that came to water: the first of them was shot, so the last of them fled; lay down a precedent today and change tomorrow. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fifty in this expedition of ours, and fifty when we return."" And that was on one of his journeys. And Muhallim is a tall, brown, striking man, at the edge of the people. He said: They kept at him until he stood and sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his eyes shedding tears, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what has reached you has happened, and I repent to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You killed him with your weapon at the beginning of Islam. O Allah, do not forgive Muhallim, in a loud voice. He said that three times, each time saying: ""You killed him with your weapon at the beginning of Islam. O Allah, do not forgive Muhallim."""
"5462","5456 - Narrated to us Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, who said: When he died, his people buried him, and the earth cast him out three times, so they threw him between the outskirts of a mountain and piled stones over him, and wild beasts ate him. Ibn Abi al-Zinad said: It reached me that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told the earth had cast him out, he said: The earth accepts one worse than him, but Allah wished to show you the gravity of bloodshed in His sight."
"5463","5457 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, who said: I heard Ziyad ibn Sa'd ibn Dumayrah al-Sulami narrating to 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr - my father and my grandfather narrated to me, and they had been present at Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - both saying: The Messenger of Allah led us in Zuhr prayer, then sat in the shade of a tree. Then al-Aqra' ibn Habis and 'Uyaynah ibn Badr stood; 'Uyaynah ibn Hisn demanded the blood of the Ashja'i, 'Amir ibn al-Adbat, and he was that day the chief of Qays, while al-Aqra' ibn Habis defended Muhallim ibn Jaththamah for Khindif. They disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""You take the blood-money, fifty in this journey of ours, and fifty when we return."" Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"5464","537 - Sa'd ibn Abi Dhubab al-Dawsi. 5458 - Narrated to us Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba', (Ha) and narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Abu 'Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam, (Ha) and narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father narrated to me, and Bakr ibn Khalaf, (Ha) and narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam, and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, both saying: Narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, all saying: Narrated to us Safwan ibn 'Isa, narrated to us al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Munir ibn 'Abd Allah, from his father, from his grandfather Sa'd ibn Abi Dhubab, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accepted Islam, and said: O Messenger of Allah, assign to my people what they have accepted Islam upon. So he did, and appointed me over them. And Abu Bakr appointed me after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and 'Umar appointed me after Abu Bakr. So I said to my people: There is no good in wealth whose charity is not paid, so pay the zakah of honey. They said: How much do you see? I said: A tenth. So I took a tenth from them, and brought it to 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he sold it and placed it among the charities of the Muslims."
"5465","538 - Sa'd ibn 'Umarah al-Sa'di, ""and he used to reside in Madinah."" 5459 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Khattab al-Tustari, narrated to us 'Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm and Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Qays al-Ansari narrated to me, that both narrated to him from Sa'd ibn 'Umarah, brother of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr, and he had companionship, that a man said to him: Advise me concerning myself, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: ""When you stand for prayer, perform ablution fully, for there is no prayer for one without ablution, and no faith for one without prayer."" Then he said: ""When you pray, pray the prayer of one bidding farewell, and abandon seeking many needs, for it is present poverty; and gather despair of what is in people's hands, for it is wealth; and consider what you would apologize for, of word and deed, and avoid it."""
"5466","539 - Sa'd ibn Tamim, Abu Bilal al-Sakuni, ""he used to reside in Sham at Damascus."" 5460 - Narrated to us Abu Zur'ah 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Umar, narrated to us Abu Mushir, (Ha) and narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi, and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying: Narrated to us Hisham ibn 'Ammar, both saying: Narrated to us Sadaqah ibn Khalid, narrated to us 'Amr ibn Sharahil al-'Ansi, from Bilal ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of your ummah is best? He said: ""I and my contemporaries."" We said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Then the second generation."" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Then the third generation."" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Then there will be a people who swear though not asked to swear, and testify though not asked to testify, and are trusted but do not fulfill."""
"5467","5461 - Narrated to us Abu 'Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi, (Ha). And narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Irq al-Himsi, and 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying: Narrated to us 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak, both saying: Narrated to us al-Walid ibn Muslim, narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn al-'Ala ibn Zabr, from Bilal ibn Sa'd, from his father - and he had companionship - who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is due to the caliph after you? He said: ""What is due to me: showing mercy to kin, being just in apportioning, and being fair in distribution."""
"5468","5462 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi, narrated to us Hibban ibn Musa, narrated to us Ibn al-Mubarak, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Bilal ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Where are your sons?"" I said: Here they are. He said: ""Then bring them to me."" So I commanded my family and they dressed them in white shirts, then I brought them to him. He said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You for them from disbelief and misguidance, and from the poverty that befalls the sons of Adam."
"5469","540 - Sa'd ibn Khawlah; of Badr. 5463 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those who were present at Badr among Banu 'Amir ibn Lu'ayy, then among Banu Malik ibn Hisl: Sa'd ibn Khawlah."""
"5470","5464 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr, and he read to me the hadith of Subay'ah, that her husband died. He said: Her husband was Sa'd ibn Khawlah, and Sa'd ibn Khawlah died in Makkah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said during his visit to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas in the Farewell Hajj: O Allah, complete for my companions their emigration, and do not turn them back on their heels; but the wretched Sa'd ibn Khawlah - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expressed pity for him that he died in Makkah."
"5471","Sa'd ibn al-Atwal al-Juhani; he used to reside in Basra. 5465 - Narrated to us Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari, narrated to us Shabab al-'Usfuri, who said: ""Sa'd ibn al-Atwal ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Wahib ibn 'Attab ibn Malik ibn Sa'd ibn Sa'bah ibn 'Adi ibn 'Awf ibn Ghatafan ibn Qays ibn Juhaynah ibn Zayd, of the residents of Basra."""
"5472","What Sa'd ibn al-Atwal transmitted as musnad. 5466 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both saying: Narrated to us Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, (Ha) and narrated to us Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-'Abbadani, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb, (Ha) and narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us 'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi, all saying: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, 'Abd al-Malik Abu Ja'far al-Madani informed me, from Abu Nadrah, from Sa'd ibn al-Atwal, that his brother died leaving three hundred dirhams and leaving dependents. So I wanted to spend it on his dependents, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother is held back by his debt, so settle it on his behalf. So I settled it on his behalf, then said: O Messenger of Allah, I have paid on his behalf except two dinars claimed by a woman who has no proof. He said: ""Give them to her, for she is truthful."""
"5473","5467 - Narrated to us 'Abdan ibn Ahmad, narrated to us Wasil ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Badr ibn Asl ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn al-Atwal, my father 'Abd Allah ibn Badr narrated to me, who said: 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'd would go out to his companions in Tustar and visit them, staying the day of his arrival and the second, and leaving on the third. It would be said to him: Would that you stayed. He would say: I heard my father saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me lingering; whoever settles in the land of kharaj has lingered, and I dislike staying."
"5474","Sa'd, Abu al-Harith. 5468 - Narrated to us Idris ibn Ja'far al-'Attar, narrated to us 'Uthman ibn 'Umar, narrated to us Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Khuzamah, from al-Harith ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about incantations with which we seek healing and medicines with which we treat: do they repel any of the decree of Allah? He said: ""They are part of the decree of Allah."" Thus 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated it from Yunus, while others differed and narrated it from Yunus as others narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Khuzamah."
"5475","543 - Sa'd ibn Muhayyisah, Abu Haram al-Ansari. 5469 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Muhayyisah, from his father, that a she-camel of al-Bara ibn 'Azib entered a man's orchard and caused damage in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that owners of property must guard it by day, and owners of livestock must guard them by night."
"5476","5470 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us Mu'alla ibn Asad al-'Ammi, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ma'mar, al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, and Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Haram ibn Muhayyisah, that a she-camel of al-Bara ibn 'Azib entered the people's orchard and damaged their crops. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that owners of livestock must guard their livestock by night, and owners of crops must guard their crops by day."
"5477","5471 - Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Ibn Shihab, from Haram ibn Muhayyisah, from his father, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the earnings of the cupper, and he forbade him it. So he complained to him of need, and he said: ""Feed it to your watering camels."""
"5478","544 - Sa'd ibn Suwayd al-Ansari; martyred on the day of Uhud. 5472 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those martyred on the day of Uhud among the Ansar, then among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Sa'd ibn Suwayd."""
"5479","545 - Sa'd ibn Salamah al-Ansari, ""martyred on the day of the Bridge of al-Mada'in, in the year fifteen."" 5473 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those killed on the day of the Bridge of al-Mada'in with Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas among the Ansar, then among Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal ibn Za'ura: Sa'd ibn Salamah."""
"5480","5474 - Narrated to us Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani, narrated to us Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: ""In the naming of those killed on the day of the Bridge among the Ansar, then among Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, then among Banu Za'ura: Sa'd ibn Salamah."""
"5481","546 - Sa'd ibn Yazid al-Ansari; of Badr, and it is said: ""Sa'd ibn 'Uthman."" 5475 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu Zurayq: Sa'd ibn Yazid ibn Khaldah ibn 'Amir ibn Zurayq."""
"5482","5476 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Sulayman, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu Zurayq: Sa'd ibn 'Uthman ibn Khaldah ibn Makhlad."""
"5483","547 - Sa'd ibn Suhayl al-Ansari; of Badr. 5477 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu Dinar ibn al-Najjar: Sa'd ibn Suhayl ibn 'Abd al-Ashhal ibn Harithah ibn Dinar ibn al-Najjar."""
"5484","548 - Sa'd al-Akhram, ""he used to reside in Kufah, and there is disagreement concerning his companionship."" 5478 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Abu Kurayb, and 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, (Ha) and narrated to us Musa ibn Harun, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr, all saying: Narrated to us Yahya ibn 'Isa, from al-A'mash, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from al-Mughirah ibn Sa'd ibn al-Akhram, from his father or from his uncle - al-A'mash doubts - who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, guide me to a deed that brings me near Paradise and distances me from the Fire. He was silent for a while, then raised his head to the sky and looked, then said: Worship Allah without associating anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, love for people what you love to be given to you, and what you dislike to be given to you, keep people free of it."
"5485","550 - Sa'd ibn Abi Rafi'. 5479 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Yunus ibn al-Hajjaj al-Thaqafi, narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: Sa'd ibn Abi Rafi' said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me visiting me in illness, and placed his hand between my breasts until I felt its coolness upon my heart, and said: You are a man afflicted in the heart; go to al-Harith ibn Kaladah, for he is a man who practices medicine. Let him take five dates of the 'ajwah of Madinah, crush them with their stones, then rub you with them."
"5486","551 - Sa'd al-Zafari, ""he used to reside in Madinah."" 5480 - Narrated to us Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-'Attar al-Makki, narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, narrated to us Abu Damrah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Sa'd al-Zafari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, and said: ""I dislike scalding remedies."""
"5487","552 - Sa'd ibn al-Mundhir al-Ansari, ""he used to reside in Madinah."" 5481 - Narrated to us Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri, narrated to us Yahya ibn Bukayr, narrated to us Ibn Lahi'ah, Habban ibn Wasi' narrated to me, from Sa'd ibn al-Mundhir al-Ansari, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I recite the Qur'an in three days? He said: ""Yes, if you are able."" So he would recite it thus until he died."
"5488","553 - Sa'd ibn Junadah al-'Awfi, ""he used to reside in Kufah."" 5482 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mabhram al-Idhaji, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Marzuq, narrated to us Sa'd ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Atiyyah ibn Sa'd ibn Junadah al-'Awfi, my uncle al-Husayn ibn Hasan ibn 'Atiyyah narrated to me, Yunus ibn Nufay', judge of Baghdad, narrated to me, Sa'd ibn Junadah narrated to us, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he taught me: When the earth is shaken, and: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One. And he taught me: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest. And he said: ""They are the lasting righteous deeds."""
"5489","5483 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Najiyah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-'Awfi, my father narrated to me, my uncle al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Nufay' al-Jadali, from Sa'd ibn Junadah, who said: I was among the first of the people of Ta'if to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I left my family in al-Sarah in the morning and reached Mina in the afternoon, then climbed the mountain, then descended, and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I accepted Islam, and he taught me: Say, He is Allah, One, and: When the earth is shaken with its shaking. And he taught me these words: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest. And he said: They are the lasting righteous deeds."
"5490","5484 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Najiyah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-'Awfi, my father narrated to me, my uncle al-Husayn narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Nufay' al-Jadali, from Sa'd ibn Junadah, who said: I was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Hunayn, and I heard him saying: Whoever stands the night, performs ablution, rinses his mouth, then says: Glory be to Allah a hundred times, praise be to Allah a hundred times, there is no god but Allah a hundred times, and Allah is Greatest a hundred times, his sins are forgiven, except bloodshed and wealth, for they are not annulled."
"5491","5485/1 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Najiyah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-'Awfi, my father narrated to us, my uncle al-Husayn narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Nufay', from Sa'd ibn Junadah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished at Hunayn, we stopped in a barren land with nothing in it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather; whoever finds a stick, let him bring it, and whoever finds a bone or anything, let him bring it. He said: It was only an hour before we made it a heap. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do you see this? Thus sins gather upon a man among you as you have gathered this. So let a man fear Allah and not commit a sin, minor or major, for it is recorded against him."""
"5492","5485/2 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Najiyah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-'Awfi, my father narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, Yunus ibn Nufay' narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Junadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has married me in Paradise to Maryam, daughter of 'Imran, the wife of Pharaoh, and the sister of Musa."
"5493","5486/1 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sa'd, my father narrated to us, my uncle al-Husayn narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Nufay', from Sa'd ibn Junadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs of the sea are better in the sight of Allah than the martyrs of the land."
"5494","5486/2 - Narrated to us 'Abd Allah ibn Najiyah, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-'Awfi, my father narrated to us, my uncle al-Husayn narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Nufay', from Sa'd ibn Junadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever separates from the community is in the Fire upon his face; for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Who answers the distressed when he calls upon Him, removes evil, and makes you successors on earth. So succession is from Allah: if it is good, He takes it away with him, and if it is evil, he is seized for it. Upon you is obedience in what Allah, Exalted, has commanded you."
"5495","554 - Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd ibn al-Nu'man al-Ansari, the reciter; of Badr. 5487 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among Banu Sawwad ibn Ka'b - and Ka'b's name is Zafar: Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd ibn al-Nu'man."""
"5496","5488 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr, then among al-Aws, then among Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, then among Banu Umayyah ibn Zayd: Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd ibn al-Nu'man."""
"5497","5489 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr saying: ""Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd is Abu Zayd, and he is the one who compiled the Qur'an, and his son is 'Umayr ibn Sa'd, governor of 'Umar; and he is Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd ibn al-Nu'man."""
"5498","5490 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr saying: ""Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd was killed at al-Qadisiyyah in the year sixteen."""
"5499","5491 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Sufyan, from Qays ibn Muslim, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd was called the reciter in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5500","5492 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, narrated to us 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us Hushaym, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, and Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, who said: Six of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), all of the Ansar, compiled the Qur'an: Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, Zayd ibn Thabit, Abu Zayd, and Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd. Al-Hafiz Ibn Hajar said: ""'Ali ibn al-Madini mentioned that his name is Aws, and from Yahya ibn Ma'in he is Thabit ibn Zayd, and it is said he is Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd ibn al-Nu'man, and al-Tabarani affirmed this from his shaykh Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah, who said: and he is the one called the reciter, he was over al-Qadisiyyah and was martyred there, and he is the father of 'Umayr ibn Sa'd. And from al-Waqidi: he is Qays ibn al-Sakan ibn Qays ibn Za'ur ibn Haram al-Ansari al-Najjari, supported by the saying of Anas: 'One of my uncles,' for he is of the tribe of Banu Haram."" [al-Fath (11/122)]."
"5501","5493 - Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Qays ibn Muslim, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, (Ha). And narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Hamid, narrated to us Qays ibn al-Rabi', from Qays ibn Muslim, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd, the like."
"5502","555 - Sa'd ibn al-Nu'man al-Ansari; of Badr. 5494 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those of the Ansar who were present at Badr: Sa'd ibn al-Nu'man ibn Qays ibn 'Amr ibn Zayd ibn Umayyah."""
"5503","556 - Sa'd, freedman of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, ""he used to reside in Basra."" 5495 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Riyahi, narrated to us 'Amir ibn Salih ibn Rustum, from his father, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd, freedman of Abu Bakr, who said: A man complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal, who used to say this poetry. He said: O Messenger of Allah, Safwan has lampooned me. He said: Leave Safwan, for Safwan is foul of tongue but sound of heart."
"5504","5496 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Riyahi, narrated to us 'Amir ibn Salih, from his father, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd, freedman of Abu Bakr, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I think he said: on a journey - and we stopped at a place. He said to me: O Sa'd, go to that goat and milk it. And my memory of that place was that there was no goat in it. So I came to him and there was a goat full of milk, so I milked it - I do not know how many times - then I entrusted it to a man, and I became busy with the baggage, and the goat went away. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waited for me and said: ""Where, Sa'd?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, the baggage kept us busy, and the goat went away. He said: ""The goat was taken away by its Lord."""
"5505","5497 - Narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, narrated to us 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab, narrated to us 'Amir ibn Salih, from his father, from al-Hasan, who said: Sa'd said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we had some dates with us. Safwan said to me: Feed me these dates. I said: They are few dates, and I am not sure he will call for them, and when they stop you will eat with them. He said: Feed me, for hunger has destroyed me, and mentioned what it had done to him. I refused him that, so he hamstrung the camel carrying the dates. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Tell Safwan to go away. He said: So that night he did not spend but going around the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came to 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Where shall I go? Shall I go to disbelief? So 'Ali came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that. He said: ""Tell Safwan to rejoin."""
"5506","5498 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddam, narrated to us Abu Dawud, narrated to us Abu 'Amir al-Khazzaz, from al-Hasan, from Sa'd, freedman of Abu Bakr, who said: I brought dates to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they would eat before him and eat two together. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining two dates together."
"5507","557 - Sa'd ibn Himman, and it is also said: Ibn Himar, al-Ansari, ""martyred on the day of al-Yamamah."" 5499 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Fulayh, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab: ""In the naming of those martyred on the day of al-Yamamah among the Ansar, then among Banu Sa'idah: Sa'd ibn Himar, an ally of theirs."""
"5508","558 - Sa'd ibn Harithah al-Ansari; martyred on the day of al-Yamamah. 5500 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those martyred on the day of al-Yamamah among the Ansar, then among Banu Sa'idah: Sa'd ibn Harithah ibn Lawdhan ibn 'Abd Wudd."""
"5509","559 - Sa'd ibn Habban al-Balawi, ""ally of the Ansar, martyred on the day of al-Yamamah, an ally of theirs."" 5501 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Urwah: ""In the naming of those martyred on the day of al-Yamamah among the Ansar, then among Banu Sa'idah: Sa'd ibn Habban, an ally of theirs from Bali."""
"5510","560 - Sa'd ibn al-Midhas. 5502 - Narrated to us 'Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq, narrated to us Nasr ibn 'Alqamah, (Ha) and narrated to us Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi, narrated to us Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Bahrani, Nasr ibn 'Alqamah informed us, from his father, from Nasr, from his brother, from Ibn 'A'idh, who said: Sa'd ibn al-Midhas said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever knows something, let him not conceal it; and whoever's eyes shed tears from fear of Allah, it is not lawful for him to enter the Fire ever, except the passing touch of the Merciful; and whoever lies about me, let him take a house in Hell."
"5511","Sa'd, the freedman of Hatib ibn Abi Balta'a: a participant at Badr, martyred on the day of Uhud. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr: Sa'd, the freedman of Hatib ibn Abi Balta'a."
"5512","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr: Sa'd, the freedman of Hatib ibn Abi Balta'a."
"5513","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those Muslims who were martyred on the day of Uhud: Sa'd, the freedman of Hatib ibn Abi Balta'a."
"5514","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Ishaq ibn Isa al-Tabba' from Abu Ma'shar, who said: Sa'd ibn Khawli, the freedman of Hatib ibn Abi Balta'a, a man of Madhhij."
"5515","Sa'd, the freedman of Khawli: a participant at Badr. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr: Sa'd, the freedman of Khawli, of Banu Amir ibn Lu'ayy."
"5516","Those whose name is Sa'id. Sa'id ibn Amir ibn Hidhyam al-Jumahi: he used to reside in Hims; he is Sa'id ibn Amir ibn Hidhyam ibn Salaman ibn Rabi'a ibn Harqus ibn Sa'd ibn Jumah, and his mother was Arwa bint Abi Mu'ayt ibn Abi Amr ibn Umayya ibn Abd Shams. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi from Mas'ud ibn Sa'd from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, sent to Sa'id ibn Amir al-Jumahi: We are appointing you over these people; march with them to the land of the enemy and strive with them - then he mentioned a long hadith, saying in it: Sa'id said: I will not stay behind from the first company after I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say regarding the poor Muslims: They are brought forth honored as doves are honored, and it is said to them: Stand for reckoning; they say: By Allah, we left nothing to be reckoned for; Allah, mighty and majestic, says: My servants have spoken the truth; so the poor believers enter Paradise seventy years before the people."
"5517","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Ibn Sabit from Sa'id ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5518","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Bistam al-Za'farani from Abu Kurayb from Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida from Shu'ba from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Ibn Sabit, who said: Sa'id ibn Amir said: I will not stay behind from the first company after what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The poor Muslims will come on the Day of Resurrection upon their saddles, and it is said to them: Stand for reckoning; they say: You gave us nothing to be reckoned for; so they enter Paradise forty years before the people."
"5519","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Yahya ibn Ma'in, with another chain, and al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Asbahani narrated to us from Ja'far ibn Sari' al-Kufi, both saying: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us from Musa al-Saghir from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit from Sa'id ibn Amir ibn Hidhyam, who said: It reached Umar that he kept nothing in his house out of need, so he sent him ten thousand; he took it and began distributing it in purses. His wife said to him: Where are you taking this? He said: I am taking it to one who will give us profit on it. He left almost nothing of it, and when what they had ran out, his wife said to him: Go to some of your companions whom you gave, that they may give you back from their profits. He kept putting her off until it went on long, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If a houri were to show a finger of her fingers, every living soul would smell her fragrance; so I am leaving them; but by Allah, you are more deserving that I leave you for them than they for you."
"5520","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasa al-Warraq from Sayyar ibn Hatim from Ja'far ibn Sulayman and al-Harith ibn Nabhan, from Malik ibn Dinar from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Sa'id ibn Amir ibn Hidhyam, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If a woman of the people of Paradise were to look down upon the people of the earth, she would fill the earth with the scent of musk and would take away the light of the sun and the moon; and by Allah, I would not choose you over them; and he pushed her chest, meaning his wife."
"5521","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqba al-Shaybani al-Kufi from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani from Shababa ibn Sawwar from Abu Abd Allah al-Bahili from Ghiyath ibn Sufyan from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit from Sa'id ibn Amir al-Jumahi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: O Abu Bakr, come, and O Umar, come; I have been commanded to establish brotherhood between you two by revelation sent down to me from heaven; you are two brothers in this world, two brothers in Paradise; let each of you greet his companion and shake his hand. So Abu Bakr took Umar's hand, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: He will be before him; he will die before him. And he said: O Zubayr, O Talha, come; I have been commanded to establish brotherhood between you two; you are two brothers in this world, two brothers in Paradise; let each of you greet his companion. So they did. Then he said: O Ali, come, O Ammar, come; I have been commanded to establish brotherhood between you two; you are two brothers in this world, two brothers in Paradise; let each of you greet his companion. So they did. Then he said the like of that to Ubayy ibn Ka'b and to Ibn Mas'ud, and they did; then he said the like of that to Abu al-Darda and to Salman, and they did; then he said the like of that to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas and to Suhayb, and they did; then the like of that to Abu Dharr and to Bilal, the freedman of al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, and they did. Then he said: O Usama, and O Abu Hind, come - a cupper who used to cup the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would drink his blood - come. So he said the like of that to them, and the like of that to Abu Ayyub and to Abd Allah ibn Salam, and they did. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"5522","Sa'id ibn al-As ibn Sa'id ibn al-As ibn Umayya ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Yahya ibn Ya'la ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi from his father from Ghaylan ibn Jami' from Abu Ishaq from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, who said: Uthman said: Which people are most eloquent? They said: Sa'id ibn al-As."
"5523","What Sa'id ibn al-As narrated. Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Isma'il ibn Abi Uways from his brother from Sulayman ibn Bilal from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab: Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn al-As informed me, saying: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on his bed, wearing the cloak of A'isha, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he gave Abu Bakr permission while in that state, then he conveyed his need to him, then left. Then Umar asked permission, and he gave him permission while in that state, then he conveyed his need to him, then left. Uthman said: Then I asked his permission, so he sat up and gathered his clothes about him; I conveyed my need to him, then left. A'isha said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you not stir for Abu Bakr and Umar as you stirred for Uthman? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uthman is a modest man, and I feared that if I gave him permission while in that state, he would not fully convey his need."
"5524","Narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri from Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli from Salama ibn Rawh from Aqil from Ibn Shihab: Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn al-As informed me that Sa'id ibn al-As informed him that Abu Bakr asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on his bed, wearing the cloak of A'isha; so he gave Abu Bakr permission while in that state, and Abu Bakr conveyed his need, then left. Then Umar asked permission while in that state, conveyed his need, then left. Uthman said: Then I asked permission, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat up and gathered his clothes about him; then I conveyed my need to him, then left. A'isha said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you not stir for Abu Bakr and Umar as you stirred for Uthman? He said: Uthman is a modest man, and I feared that if I gave him permission while in that state, he would not convey his need to me."
"5525","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Abd al-Razzaq from Umar ibn Habib from Isma'il ibn Umayya from his father from his grandfather, who said: We had a boy called Dhakwan or Tahman, and he had a slave; so he freed half of him, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He is freed in your freeing and enslaved in your enslaving."
"5526","Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya al-Abdashi from Abu Umayya al-Ta'ifi, of the descendants of Sa'id ibn al-As, from his grandfather, from his grandfather Sa'id ibn al-As: Abu Uhayha, his grandfather, was ill when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent; so he said in his illness: Do not lift me from my bed; the son of Abu Kabsha shall not turn to me in Mecca. His son, standing at his head, said: O Allah, do not lift him."
"5527","Narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki from Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya from Abu Umayya al-Ta'ifi from his grandfather, from his grandfather Sa'id ibn al-As: Uthman ibn Maz'un said: O Messenger of Allah, give me permission for castration. He said to him: O Uthman, Allah has replaced monasticism for us with the easy Hanifiyya, and takbir upon every eminence; so if you are of us, do as we do."
"5528","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Minjab ibn al-Harith from Khallad ibn Isa al-Ahwal from Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn al-As from his father from his grandfather, who said: Bakr ibn Wa'il came to Mecca, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go to them and present me to them. Abu Bakr went to them and said: Which people are you? They said: Banu Dhuhl ibn Tha'laba. He said: It is not you I want; you are the tails. Daghfal stood up to him and said: And who are you? He said: A man of Quraysh. He said: Of Banu Hashim? He said: No. He said: Then of Banu Umayya? He said: No. He said: Then you are of the tails? Then Abu Bakr returned to them a second time and said: Which people are you? They said: Banu Dhuhl ibn Shayban. He said: It is you I want; so he presented to them. They said: Until our elder so-and-so comes - Khallad said: I think he said: al-Muthanna ibn Kharja - so when their elder came, Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, presented to them. He said: Between us and the Persians there is war; when we are done with what is between us and them, we will return and consider what you say. Abu Bakr said: If you defeat them, will you follow us in our cause? He said: We do not stipulate this for you upon us, but when we are done with what is between us and them, we will return and consider what you say. When they met on the day of Dhi Qar, they and the Persians, their elder said: What is the name of the man who called you to what he called you to? They said: Muhammad. He said: Then he is your battle cry. So they were given victory over the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Through me they were given victory."
"5529","Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn Ubada al-Ansari: he used to reside in Medina. Narrated Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar from Yazid ibn Harun from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf from Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn Ubada, who said: Among our houses was a weak, sickly, dwarfed little man; the tribe suddenly found him with one of their slave girls, behaving wickedly with her. Sa'd mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Strike him his hadd. He said: O Messenger of Allah, if we strike him a full hadd we will kill him, for he is weak. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take for him a palm-branch cluster with a hundred twigs, and strike him with it a single blow."
"5530","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abd Allah ibn Numayr from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf from Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn Ubada, who said: Among our houses was a dwarfed, weak man; he was suddenly found with a slave girl of the household, behaving wickedly with her. Sa'd raised his case to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Lash him a hundred lashes. He said: O Messenger of Allah, he is weaker than that; if struck a hundred he will die. He said: Take for him a palm-branch cluster with a hundred twigs, and strike him a single blow."
"5531","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam from Malik ibn Anas from Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Shurahbil ibn Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn Ubada from his father from his grandfather, who said: Sa'd ibn Ubada went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his campaigns, and his mother fell fatally ill in Medina. He said to her: Make a bequest. She said: Regarding what should I bequeath? The wealth is Sa'd's wealth. She died before Sa'd returned, and when Sa'd returned, that was mentioned to him. Sa'd said: O Messenger of Allah, will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. Sa'd said: Such-and-such garden is charity on her behalf, naming a garden."
"5532","Sa'id Abu Kindir. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti, with another chain, and al-Hadrami narrated to us from Wahb ibn Baqiyya, both saying: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman from Kindir ibn Sa'id from his father, who said: I performed hajj in the Jahiliyya, and there was a man circumambulating the House, chanting rajaz, saying - I said: Who is this? They said: This is Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim; camels of his were lost, so he sent his son seeking them, and he was delayed; he never sent him on an errand but he brought it back. He said: I had not moved before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, bringing the camels with him. He said: O my son, I grieved for you a grief that will never leave me."
"5533","Sa'id ibn Hurayth al-Makhzumi: he used to reside in Kufa; he is Sa'id ibn Hurayth ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Makhzum, and his mother was Atika bint Hisham ibn Hidhyam ibn Sa'd ibn Rabab ibn Sahm. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mada' al-Missisi from Khalaf ibn Tamim from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Amr ibn Hurayth, who said: My brother Sa'id was older than me."
"5534","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, who said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr say: I heard Amr ibn Hurayth say: My brother Sa'id ibn Hurayth, who had companionship with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), an excellent brother, narrated to me - I inclined toward Kufa, so I asked his permission to sell the house, and he permitted its sale. He said to me: O my brother, hold back your hand from the price of this house, and do not diminish any of it while you can, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever of you sells a house or property, it will not be blessed for him unless he puts it into the like of it. So I believed my brother's word, sought blessing in the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and bought part of this house of ours from that; Allah gave us in return what is better."
"5535","Sa'id ibn Yarbu' al-Surm al-Makhzumi: he used to reside in Medina; he is Sa'id ibn Yarbu' ibn Ankatha ibn Amir ibn Makhzum, and his mother was Hind bint Rabab ibn Sahm. Narrated Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj from Yahya ibn Bukayr, who said: Sa'id ibn Yarbu' died in the year fifty-four, at the age of a hundred and twenty."
"5536","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us from Layth ibn Harun al-Ukli, with another chain, and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban, all saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id al-Makhzumi from his grandfather, from his father Sa'id, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Which of us is older? He said: You are older and better than me, and I am earlier in age; so he named him Sa'id, and said: al-Surm is gone."
"5537","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini, with another chain, and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us from Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili, both saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id al-Makhzumi from his grandfather, from his father Sa'id - he was called al-Surm - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Mecca: Four I do not grant security to, in halal or haram: al-Huwayrith ibn Nufayl, Miqyas ibn Dubaba, Hilal ibn Khatal, and Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh. As for Huwayrith, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, killed him; as for Miqyas ibn Dubaba, a cousin of his killed him in retaliation; as for Hilal ibn Khatal, al-Zubayr killed him; as for Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh, Uthman ibn Affan sought security for him, for he was his milk-brother; and two singing girls of Miqyas who used to sing lampooning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - one of them was killed and the other escaped and became Muslim."
"5538","Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' ibn Adi ibn Malik al-Ansari: martyred on the day of Yamama. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those killed on the day of Yamama of the Ansar, then of Banu Jahjabi: Sa'id ibn Rabi' ibn Adi ibn Malik."
"5539","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Yamama of the Ansar, then of al-Aws, then of Banu Amr ibn Awf: Sa'id ibn Rabi' ibn Adi ibn Malik."
"5540","Sa'id ibn Iyas Abu Amr al-Shaybani: a mukhadram. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Isa ibn Abd Allah al-Sulami, who said: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani say: I remember that I heard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was herding camels for my family at Kazima."
"5541","Sa'id ibn Uthman ibn Khalid ibn Makhlad ibn Haritha ibn Malik ibn Adab ibn Jusham ibn al-Khazraj Abu Ubada al-Zuraqi: a participant at Badr; also said Ubada, and the correct is Abu Ubada. Narrated Mas'ada ibn Sa'd al-Attar al-Makki from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami from Abu Damra Anas ibn Iyad from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Ya'la ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abd Allah ibn Ubada al-Zuraqi narrated to him that he used to hunt sparrows at Bi'r Ihab, which belonged to them; Ubada saw me after I had taken a sparrow, took it from me and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade what is between its two lava plains."
"5542","Sa'id ibn al-Harith ibn Qays al-Qurashi then al-Sahmi: killed on the day of Ajnadayn. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those killed on the day of Ajnadayn of the Muslims, then of Quraysh, of Banu Sahm: Sa'id ibn al-Harith ibn Qays."
"5543","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those killed on the day of Ajnadayn of Quraysh, then of Banu Sahm: Sa'id ibn al-Harith ibn Qays."
"5544","Sa'id ibn Sa'id ibn al-As. Narrated Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani from Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli from Muhammad ibn Salama from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, regarding the naming of those Muslims martyred on the day of Ta'if, then of Quraysh, of Banu Umayya ibn Abd Shams: Sa'id ibn Sa'id ibn al-As."
"5545","Sa'id ibn Abi Rashid. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us from Amr ibn Mujammi' from Yunus ibn Khabbab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rashid - al-Hadrami said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'ib - from Sa'id ibn Abi Rashid, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In my umma there will be sinking, transformation, and pelting."
"5546","Sa'id Abu Abd al-Aziz, of no lineage. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Mu'alla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili from Uthman ibn Matar al-Shaybani from Abd al-Ghafur, meaning Ibn Sa'id, from Abd al-Aziz, from his father - Uthman said: His father had companionship - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rajab is a great month; Allah multiplies good deeds in it. Whoever fasts a day of Rajab, it is as if he fasted a year; whoever fasts seven days of it, seven gates of Hell are closed from him; whoever fasts eight days of it, eight gates of Paradise are opened for him; whoever fasts ten days of it, he does not ask Allah for anything but He gives it to him; whoever fasts fifteen days of it, a caller calls out in heaven: What is past has been forgiven you, so resume deeds; whoever increases, Allah, mighty and majestic, increases him. In Rajab Allah carried Nuh in the ark, so he fasted Rajab and commanded those with him to fast; the ark sailed with them six months, the end of that being the day of Ashura, when it rested upon al-Judi; so Nuh and those with him and the beasts fasted in thanks to Allah, mighty and majestic. On the day of Ashura Allah parted the sea for Banu Isra'il; on the day of Ashura Allah, mighty and majestic, turned to Adam (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and to the city of Yunus; and in it Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born."
"5547","Sa'id ibn Yazid al-Azdi. Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ya'qub ibn Humayd from Abd Allah ibn Musa from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Sa'id ibn Yazid al-Azdi, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Advise me. He said: I advise you to be shy of Allah, mighty and majestic, as you are shy of a righteous man of your people."
"5548","Sa'id ibn Ubayd al-Qari. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Qays ibn Muslim from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Sa'id ibn Ubayd - in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he was called al-Qari - that he had met an enemy and fled from them; Umar said to him: Would you go to Syria, that Allah may favor you? He said: No, except against the enemy I fled from. So he addressed them at al-Qadisiyya, saying: We shall meet the enemy tomorrow, Allah willing, and we shall be martyred; so do not wash blood from us, and do not shroud us except in the garment upon us."
"5549","Sa'id ibn Qays ibn Sakhr al-Ansari: a participant at Badr. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who attended Badr: Sa'id ibn Qays ibn Sakhr ibn Haram ibn Rabi'a ibn Adi ibn Ghanm ibn Ka'b ibn Salama."
"5550","Those whose name is Sahl. Sahl ibn Hunayf ibn Wahib - also said Ukaym - ibn Tha'laba ibn Mujadda'a ibn al-Harith ibn Amr, kunya Abu Thabit: a participant at Badr; he died in Kufa, and Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with them both, prayed over him. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who attended Badr, of Banu Sabigha ibn Zayd ibn Malik ibn Awf: Sahl ibn Hunayf ibn Wahib ibn Hakim ibn Tha'laba ibn Mujadda'a ibn al-Harith ibn Amr."
"5551","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi from Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham from Ziyad ibn Abd Allah from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who attended Badr: Sahl ibn Hunayf ibn Wahib ibn al-Ukaym ibn Tha'laba ibn Mujadda'a ibn al-Harith ibn Amr, and Amr who is called Bukhruj ibn Hanash ibn Awf ibn Amr ibn Awf."
"5552","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who attended Badr, then of Banu Sabigha ibn Zayd: Sahl ibn Hunayf."
"5553","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Abu Awana from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from al-Sha'bi from Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, prayed over Sahl ibn Hunayf and said takbir over him six times."
"5554","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Uyayna from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from al-Sha'bi from Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, prayed over Sahl ibn Hunayf and said takbir over him six times, then turned to us and said: He is a Badri."
"5555","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Uyayna from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil, who said: Ali prayed over Sahl ibn Hunayf and said takbir over him six times."
"5556","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Mu'awiya ibn Amr from Za'ida from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, prayed over Sahl ibn Hunayf and said takbir over him six times."
"5557","Narrated Abu al-Zinba' from Yahya ibn Bukayr, who said: Sahl ibn Hunayf died in Kufa in the year thirty-eight."
"5558","What Sahl ibn Hunayf narrated; Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf from his father. Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl from Abd Allah ibn Salih from Abu Shurayh that he heard Sahl ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrate from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from his heart, Allah brings him to the stations of the martyrs, even if he dies upon his bed."
"5559","Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl and al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, both saying: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us from Abu Shurayh that he heard Sahl ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrate from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not be strict with yourselves, for those before you perished only by their strictness with themselves, and you will find their remnants in monasteries and cloisters."
"5560","Narrated Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi from Abd Allah ibn Wahb from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh from Sahl ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of the martyr's blood to be shed, all his sin is forgiven except debt."
"5561","Narrated Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf and Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misriyyan, both saying: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us from Ibn Wahb from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd al-Madani, from Sahl ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5562","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from his father, with another chain, and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, with another chain, and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us from Abu Salih al-Harrani, all saying: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us from Musa ibn Jubayr al-Hadhda' from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a believer humiliated before him and does not help him, though able to help him, Allah will humiliate him before all creatures on the Day of Resurrection."
"5563","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rishdin from his father, from his father, from his grandfather Rishdin, from Amr ibn al-Harith from Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed umra and was on the road, he said: If we were to look at every fat camel and slaughter it and eat it, that they may see our strength. Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, rather call for the people's provisions, then supplicate over them, for Allah, mighty and majestic, will bless them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did so, then said: When you arrive, run the first three circuits, that they may see your strength. That day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give people glad tidings that whoever says: There is no god but Allah, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."
"5564","Narrated Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri from Yahya ibn Bukayr from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Zakariyya al-Himyari al-Iskandarani from al-Ala' ibn Kathir from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar ibn Makhrama from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: My father said: O my son, you saw us on the day of Badr, when one of us would point with his sword at the head of a mushrik and his head would fall from his body before it reached him."
"5565","Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi from Abu Sharik Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Dimad from Ibrahim ibn Abi Yahya from Safwan ibn Sulaym from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man's freedman is his brother and his cousin."
"5566","Narrated Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi from Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' from Mujammi' ibn Ya'qub from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Kirmani, who said: I heard Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrate from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out until he comes to this mosque and prays in it - meaning the mosque of Quba - it will be equal to an umra."
"5567","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Umar ibn Ali from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujra from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Kirmani, who said: I heard Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrate from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to the mosque of Quba and prays in it, it will be an umra."
"5568","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, both saying: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us from Musa ibn Ubayda from Yusuf ibn Tahman, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs wudu well, then enters the mosque of Quba and bows four rak'as in it, that will equal freeing a slave."
"5569","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd from Asim ibn Suwayd ibn Yazid ibn Jariya al-Ansari from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Kirmani from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs wudu well, then prays two rak'as in the mosque of Quba, it will be an umra for him."
"5570","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Kirmani from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5571","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, both saying: Abu Usama narrated to us from Musa ibn Ubayda from Ya'qub ibn Zayd from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Peace be upon you, ten good deeds are written for him; whoever says: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, twenty good deeds are written for him; whoever says: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, thirty good deeds are written for him."
"5572","Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali from Abu Ma'shar from Ayyub ibn Abi Umama, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: Ali came to Fatima, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the day of Uhud and said: Hold this sword of mine, for I did well with it in striking today. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you did well in fighting with it, Asim ibn Thabit, Sahl ibn Hunayf, and al-Harith ibn al-Simma did well."
"5573","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri from Abd al-Malik ibn Maslama al-Umawi from al-Mughira ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu al-Zinad from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, who said: A crippled man who had committed zina was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they struck him with a palm-branch stalk of dates."
"5574","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawra al-Baghdadi and Abu Khalifa, both saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Kathir from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two kinds of dates: al-Ju'rur and the Hubayq kind. He said: People used to aim for the worst of their fruits and bring them out in their charities, so revealed was: And do not aim for the impure of it to spend."
"5575","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Sa'id ibn Sulayman, with another chain, and Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us from Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mada'ini, both saying: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us from Sufyan ibn Husayn from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered charity; a man came with unripe clusters of this Sakhir dates and put them down. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: Who brought this? No one would come but would pour out what he had brought. So revealed was: O you who believe, spend of the good of what you earned and of what We brought forth for you from the earth, and do not aim for the impure of it to spend. That day he forbade al-Ju'rur and the Ibn al-Hubayq kind to be taken in charity. Al-Zuhri said: Two kinds of Medina dates. Abbad said: Sufyan said: al-Sakhir is al-Shis."
"5576","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani from Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani from Musa ibn A'yan from Ishaq ibn Rashid from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: A man fell ill until he became skin, and a slave girl entered upon him visiting him, and he fell upon her. Distressed by his sin, the people came visiting him, and he said: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me: I fell upon a forbidden woman, so let him establish the hadd upon me and purify me. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: If he were carried to you his bones would come apart, and if lashed he would die. He said: Take a hundred twigs and strike him a single blow."
"5577","Narrated Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri from Ahmad ibn Salih from Ibn Wahb from Abd al-Jalil ibn Humayd al-Yahsibi, that Ibn Shihab narrated to him from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf regarding the verse in which Allah, mighty and majestic, said: And do not aim for the impure of it to spend. He said: It is al-Ju'rur and the Ibn Hubayq kind; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that they be taken in charity."
"5578","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Duhaym from Abd Allah ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri from Nafi' ibn Yazid from Aqil from Ibn Shihab from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say: My soul has become wicked; rather let him say: My soul has become languid."
"5579","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rishdin and Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf, both saying: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us from Ibn Wahb from Yunus from Ibn Shihab from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say: My soul has become wicked; let him say: My soul has become languid."
"5580","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri from Abd Allah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Yunus from Ibn Shihab from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: None of you should say: My soul has become wicked; let him say: My soul has become languid."
"5581","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd from Ayyub ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Bilal from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi' from Ibn Shihab from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until, at al-Kharrar, he entered water to bathe - he was a fair-skinned man - and Amir ibn Rabi'a passed by him and said: I have never seen like today, neither the beauty of anything nor the skin of a secluded maiden. Sahl had barely stayed before he was stricken; the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was called for him and said: For what does one of you kill his brother? Whom do you suspect of it? They said: Amir ibn Rabi'a. So he called Amir and called for a vessel with water; he commanded Amir, so he washed his face in the water, the ends of his hands and his knees, and the ends of his feet. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the two sides of Amir's waist-wrapper and its inside, dipped them in the water, then poured the vessel over Sahl's head and emptied the vessel from behind him; so Sahl was released, with nothing wrong with him."
"5582","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: Amir ibn Rabi'a saw Sahl ibn Hunayf bathing and marveled at him, saying: By Allah, I have never seen like today a secluded maiden in her chamber - or he said: a maiden in her chamber. He said: He was stricken so that he could not raise his head. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Do you suspect anyone? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah, except that Amir ibn Rabi'a said such-and-such to him. He said: He called him - he called Amir ibn Rabi'a - and said: Glory be to Allah, for what does one of you kill his brother? When he sees something of his that pleases him, let him supplicate blessing for him. He said: Then he commanded him, so he washed for him: he washed his face, the outside of his hands, his elbows, his chest, the inside of his waist-wrapper, his knees, and the ends of his feet in the vessel, their outside; then he commanded that it be poured over his head, and emptied the vessel from behind him - I think he said: and he commanded him, so he sipped some sips of it - then he commanded him, so he stood and went off with the caravan."
"5583","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam from Malik, with another chain, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from al-Qa'nabi from Malik, with another chain, and Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Malik, from Ibn Shihab from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, that he said: Amir ibn Rabi'a saw Sahl ibn Hunayf bathing and said: By Allah, I have never seen like today, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. Sahl ibn Hunayf was stricken, and by Allah he could not raise his head. He said: Do you suspect anyone for him? They said: We suspect Amir ibn Rabi'a. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Amir ibn Rabi'a, rebuked him, and said: For what does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing? Wash for him. So Amir washed for him his face, hands, elbows, knees, ends of his feet, and the inside of his waist-wrapper in a bowl; then it was poured over him, and Sahl went off with nothing wrong with him."
"5584","Narrated al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi from Abd Allah ibn Salih from al-Hiql ibn Ziyad from Mu'awiya ibn Yahya al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, that Amir ibn Rabi'a, brother of Banu Adi ibn Ka'b, saw Sahl ibn Hunayf with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Kharrar bathing, and said: By Allah, I have never seen like today, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. Sahl was stricken, and he was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what of Sahl ibn Hunayf, who does not raise his head? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you suspect anyone of it? They said: Yes, Amir ibn Rabi'a passed by him while he bathed and said: By Allah, I have never seen like today, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Amir ibn Rabi'a, rebuked him, and said: For what does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing? Wash for him. So Amir ibn Rabi'a washed for him, and Sahl went off with the caravan with nothing wrong with him."
"5585","Narrated Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri from Ahmad ibn Salih from Ibn Wahb from Yunus ibn Yazid from Ibn Shihab from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari, that Amir ibn Rabi'a al-Adawi passed by Sahl while he bathed at al-Kharrar and said: By Allah, I have never seen like today, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. Sahl was stricken, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought to him; it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what of Sahl ibn Hunayf, who by Allah does not raise his head? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you suspect anyone of it? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, Amir ibn Rabi'a passed by him while he bathed and said: By Allah, I have never seen like today at all, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Amir ibn Rabi'a, rebuked him, and said: For what does one of you kill his brother? If you do not invoke blessing, wash for him. So Amir washed for him, and Sahl went off with the caravan. Ibn Shihab said: The washing our scholars did as we knew it: the man who brings relief to his companion is brought with a bowl of water, held for him raised from the ground; the one bringing relief puts his right hand in the water and pours one pour over his face into the bowl, then puts his left in the water and washes his right hand one pour into the bowl, then puts his right hand in and washes his left hand one pour up to the elbows, then puts both hands together in the water and washes his chest one pour into the bowl, then puts his left hand in and scoops water and pours it over the back of his right hand one pour into the bowl, then puts his left hand in and pours over the elbow of his right hand one pour into the bowl, holding it in his hand up to his neck, then does the like with the elbow of his left hand, then does the like with the back of his right foot, from the roots of the toes, and the left likewise, then puts his left hand in and pours over the back of his right knee, then does the like with the left, then dips the inside of his right waist-wrapper, then the one in whose hand is the bowl stands with the bowl and pours it over the back of the envied one's right knee - then the one in whose hand is the bowl stands with the bowl and pours it over the head of the envied one from behind him - then empties the bowl upon the ground behind him."
"5586","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, both saying: Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Ibn Shihab from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, that Amir ibn Rabi'a passed by him while he bathed and said: I have never seen, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. He was stricken so severely from pain that he could not pray. That was reported to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him, rebuked him, and said: You have killed him; for what does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a large bucket of water and said: Wash him. So he washed, and went out with the caravan."
"5587","Narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri from Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ayli from Salama ibn Rawh from Aqil from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab, that Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari informed him that Amir ibn Rabi'a informed him that he passed by Sahl ibn Hunayf while he bathed at al-Kharrar and said: By Allah, I have never seen like today at all, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. Sahl was stricken by it, and the Messenger of Allah was brought to him; it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what of Sahl ibn Hunayf, who by Allah does not raise his head? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you suspect anyone of it? They said: Yes, Amir ibn Rabi'a passed by him while he bathed and said: By Allah, I have never seen like today at all, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Amir, rebuked him, and said to him: For what does one of you kill his brother? And not invoke blessing? Wash for him. So Amir washed, and Sahl went off with the caravan."
"5588","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qa'nabi from Malik, from Muhammad ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, that he heard his father say: Sahl ibn Hunayf bathed at al-Kharrar, removing a cloak he had on, while Amir ibn Rabi'a watched. He was a white man of handsome skin, so Amir said to him: I have never seen like today, nor the skin of a virgin. Sahl fell ill on the spot, and his illness grew severe. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought to him and informed that Sahl had fallen ill and would not travel with you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him, and Sahl informed him of what had happened with Amir. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For what does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing? The evil eye is real. Perform wudu for him. So Amir performed wudu for him, and Sahl went off with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with nothing wrong with him."
"5589","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani and Jubara ibn Mughallis, both saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us from Maslama ibn Khalid al-Ansari from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, that he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his campaigns; he passed by a pond and bathed in it - he was a man of handsome body - and a man of the Ansar passed by him and said: I have never seen like today, nor the skin of a secluded maiden - marveling at his build - so he was stricken and carried borne to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He asked him, and he informed him of what the Ansari had said, saying: So-and-so passed by me and said such-and-such. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevents one of you, when he sees of his brother what pleases him of himself or his wealth, from invoking blessing upon him? For the evil eye is real."
"5590","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal from Ya'qub ibn Humayd from al-Mughira ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Ma'shar from Abd Allah ibn Abi Habiba from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, who said: I entered al-Kharrar to bathe, and Amir ibn Rabi'a said: I have never seen like today a build and color, as if the build of a secluded maiden. I was stricken and fevered. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: For what does one of you kill his brother? When something of his brother pleases him, let him supplicate blessing. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to wash his face, hands, the edge of his waist-wrapper, and his knees; then he drank of it and poured over him, and he went off with the people."
"5591","Narrated Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Hajjaj al-Zubaydi from Abu Humma Muhammad ibn Yusuf from Abu Qurra, who said: Zam'a ibn Salih mentioned from Ya'qub ibn Ata' from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited As'ad ibn Zurara, ill with a pain called al-Shawka, and cauterized him on his shoulder; so he died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An evil death for the Jews, who say: His companion treated him but did not benefit him."
"5592","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited As'ad ibn Zurara, who had a pain called al-Shawka, and cauterized him on his shoulder; so he died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A bad death for the Jews, who say: His companion treated him - did it not benefit him?"
"5593","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Arzani from Ibrahim ibn Sadaqa from Sufyan ibn Husayn from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in his room, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked out from the lattice of the house and saw - with him a comb - and said: If I knew you were watching me, I would have stood until I put this into your eyes; permission is only to restrain sight."
"5594","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, both saying: Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated to us from Sufyan ibn al-Husayn from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the poor of the people of Medina and attend their funerals when they died. A woman of the people of al-Awali died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When she is ready, inform me. They came to inform him and found him asleep, well into the night; they disliked waking him and feared for him the darkness of night and the vermin of the earth, so they went with her. When morning came he asked about her; they said: O Messenger of Allah, we came to inform you and found you asleep; we disliked waking you and feared for you the darkness of night and the vermin of the earth. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked to her grave, prayed over her, and said takbir four times; the wording is of Uthman's hadith."
"5595","Narrated Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani from his grandfather Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb from Musa ibn A'yan from Ishaq ibn Rashid from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, who said: A man among us fell ill until he became skin upon bone; a slave girl entered upon him visiting him, and he fell upon her. He said to the people visiting him: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for I fell upon a forbidden woman; let him establish the hadd upon me to purify me. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then said: By Allah, if he were carried to you his bones would come apart, and if struck he would die. He said: Take a hundred twigs of a palm cluster and strike him a single blow."
"5596","Narrated al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Mahdi al-Akhmimi al-Misri from his uncle Muhammad ibn Mahdi from Anbasa from Yunus from al-Zuhri from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Khadija bint Khuwaylid in Mecca; before him she was under Atiq ibn A'idh al-Makhzumi. Then he married A'isha in Mecca; he married no virgin besides her. Then he married Hafsa bint Umar in Medina; before him she was under Khunays ibn Hudhafa al-Sahmi. Then he married Sawda bint Zam'a; before him she was under al-Sakan ibn Amr, brother of Banu Amir ibn Lu'ayy. Then he married Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan; before him she was under Ubayd Allah ibn Jahsh al-Asadi, of Asad Khuzayma. Then he married Umm Salama bint Abi Umayya - her name was Hind; before him she was under Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza. Then he married Zaynab bint Jahsh; before him she was under Zayd ibn Haritha. Then he married Maymuna bint al-Harith. He took Juwayriya bint al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar captive, of Banu al-Mustaliq, of Khuza'a, in his campaign in which he destroyed Manat, the campaign of al-Muraysi'. He took Safiyya bint Huyayy ibn Akhtab captive, of Banu al-Nadir; both were of what Allah granted him, so he apportioned for them. He took Rayhana of Banu Qurayza as concubine, then freed her, and she joined her people and veiled while with her people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced al-Aliya bint Zibyan, parted from the sister of Banu Amr ibn Kilab, and parted from the sister of Banu al-Jawn al-Kindiyya, because of whiteness upon her. Zaynab bint Khuzayma al-Hilaliyya died while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive. It reached us that al-Aliya bint Zibyan married before Allah forbade his wives, marrying a cousin of hers of her people, and bore children among them."
"5597","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzar al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi from Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi from Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar from his father from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who draws near his wife and emits madhiy. He said: He washes his private part and performs wudu. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what of the garment is affected by it? He said: He seeks out its place and washes it."
"5598","Abd Allah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf from his father. Narrated Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi from Abu Hudhayfa, with another chain, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, all saying: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, all saying: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Abd Allah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, that Sahl ibn Hunayf narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever helps a mujahid in the path of Allah, or a debtor in his hardship, or a mukatab regarding his neck, Allah shades him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His."
"5599","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani from Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us from Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Abd Allah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever helps a mujahid in the path of Allah, or a debtor in his hardship, or a mukatab regarding his neck, Allah, mighty and majestic, shades him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His."
"5600","Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari from Sahl ibn Hunayf. Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Sa'id ibn Sulayman from Abu Ma'shar from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: The people of al-Aliya said: O Messenger of Allah, we must have sittings. He said: Then give sittings their due. They said: What is the due of sittings? He said: Much remembrance of Allah, guiding the way, and lowering the gaze."
"5601","Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq from Sahl ibn Hunayf. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim from Hammad ibn Zayd from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Sa'id ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq from his father from Sahl ibn Hunayf that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhiy. He said: Wudu suffices you for it. He said: What do I do with what hit my garment? He said: You take a handful of water and sprinkle your garment where you see it hit."
"5602","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Isma'il ibn Ulayya and Yazid ibn Harun, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Sa'id ibn Ubayd al-Sabbaq from his father from Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: I suffered greatly from madhiy and used to bathe often because of it; so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Wudu alone suffices you for that - Yazid added: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of what hits my garment of it? He said: A handful of water alone suffices you; you sprinkle your garment with it where you see it hit."
"5603","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Ibn al-Mubarak from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Sa'id ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq from his father from Sahl ibn Hunayf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5604","Uthman ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl from his grandfather. Narrated Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili from Sufyan ibn Farrukh from Yazid ibn Iyad from Ash'ath ibn Malik from Uthman ibn Abi Umama, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of the right of Jumu'a are siwak, ghusl, and whoever finds perfume let him touch of it."
"5605","Rifa'a ibn Sahl al-Juhani from Sahl ibn Hunayf. Narrated Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Asbahani from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid al-Missisi from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn Mutarrif Abu Ghassan al-Madini from Abu al-Huwayrith from Mu'awiya ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Rifa'a ibn Sahl al-Juhani, that he heard Sahl ibn Hunayf say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while coming out of one of his houses, dragging his cloak, saying: People will reach Sal'; then a time will come upon Medina when a traveler passes by some of its regions and says: This was once populous - from length of time and effacement of traces."
"5606","Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salama from Sahl ibn Hunayf. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Hudhayfa from Sufyan al-Thawri from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il, who said: Sahl ibn Hunayf said on the day of Siffin: O people, suspect opinion against religion; we saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and if we could have rebutted him we would have; we never put our swords on our shoulders in a matter but it eased us to a matter we knew, other than this matter of ours; we saw ourselves on the day of Abu Jandal, and if we could have rebutted the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we would have."
"5607","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Yahya ibn Hammad from Abu Awana from Sulayman al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il, from Sahl ibn Hunayf: Suspect opinion against religion; we saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he mentioned the hadith."
"5608","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi from Sufyan ibn Uyayna from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il, from Sahl ibn Hunayf: O people, suspect opinion against religion; we saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he mentioned the hadith."
"5609","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abu Mu'awiya from al-A'mash from Shaqiq, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Hunayf at Siffin say: O people, suspect your opinion; by Allah I saw myself on the day of Abu Jandal, and if I could rebut the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would have; by Allah we never put our swords on our shoulders toward any matter but it eased us to a matter we knew, except this matter of yours."
"5610","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Amr ibn Marzuq from Malik ibn Mighwal from Abu Husayn from Abu Wa'il, who said: Sahl ibn Hunayf arrived, so we came to him and he said: Suspect opinion against religion; I saw myself on the day of Abu Jandal, and if we could rebut the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we would have; Allah and His Messenger know best."
"5611","Narrated Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi from Ishaq ibn Shahin from Khalid from Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal from Abu Husayn from Shaqiq ibn Salama from Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: We never put our swords on our shoulders toward a matter but we came to a path that eased for us, except this matter; by Allah there is no breach on earth that we close but a worse breach opens; if you had seen me on the day of Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl, and if I could rebut the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would have; he was better than me and nobler. He said: Abu Jandal came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a Muslim, while his father was a kafir, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned him to his father, who shackled him; then he came and he returned him."
"5612","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Abd Allah ibn Numayr from Abd al-Aziz ibn Siyah from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu Wa'il, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, that he said on the day of Siffin: O people, suspect yourselves; we saw ourselves on the day of Hudaybiyya, and if we saw fighting we would have fought them. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, are we not upon truth and they upon falsehood? Are not our slain in Paradise and their slain in Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do we concede humiliation in our religion, returning before Allah has judged between us and them? He said: O Ibn al-Khattab, I am the Messenger of Allah, and He will never waste me. So he returned angry, and could not wait until he came to Abu Bakr and said: Are we not upon truth and they upon falsehood? Are not our slain in Paradise and their slain in Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do we concede humiliation in our religion, returning before Allah has judged between us and them? He said: O Ibn al-Khattab, he is the Messenger of Allah, and Allah will never waste him. Then Surat al-Fath was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Umar and recited it to him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is it a conquest? He said: Yes."
"5613","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman from Nu'aym ibn Hammad, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us from Suwayd ibn Nasr and Hibban ibn Musa, all saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Isa ibn Umar from Amr ibn Murra from Shaqiq ibn Salama, who said: Sahl ibn Hunayf said: O people, suspect your opinion; by Allah we never took hold of their legs toward a matter that cuts us but it eased us to a matter we knew, except this matter of yours, for it only increases in severity and confusion; if you had seen me on the day of Abu Jandal, and if I found helpers against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I would have objected."
"5614","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Sahl ibn Hunayf. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil from Ali ibn al-Ja'd, with another chain, and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us from Asim ibn Ali, both saying: Shu'ba narrated to us from Amr ibn Murra from Ibn Abi Layla, who said: Sahl ibn Hunayf and Qays ibn Sa'd were at al-Qadisiyya; a funeral passed by them, so they stood. It was said to them: He is only of the people of the land. They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was passed by a funeral and stood; it was said: It is the funeral of a Jew. He said: Is it not a soul?"
"5615","Yusayr ibn Amr from Sahl ibn Hunayf. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, with another chain, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us from Sahl ibn Uthman, both saying: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, both from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Yusayr ibn Amr, who said: I entered upon Sahl ibn Hunayf and said: Inform me what you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say regarding the Haruriyya. He said: I inform you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), adding nothing to you: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) striking with his hand, saying: From here - pointing with his hand - a people will emerge who recite the Qur'an, not passing their throats; they pass through Islam as an arrow passes through game."
"5616","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab, with another chain, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us from Yahya al-Himmani, all saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us from Sulayman al-Shaybani from Yusayr ibn Amr, who said: I said to Sahl ibn Hunayf: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say anything about the Khawarij? He said: I heard him say, gesturing with his hand toward Iraq: Among them a people will emerge who recite the Qur'an, not passing their throats; they pass through religion as an arrow passes through game."
"5617","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Yazid ibn Harun from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Yusayr ibn Amr, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said with his hand: A people will emerge from the east with shaven heads."
"5618","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, with another chain, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us from Sahl ibn Uthman, with another chain, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us from Yahya al-Himmani, all saying: Ali ibn Mushir informed us, with another chain, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Jarir, both from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Yusayr ibn Amr, who said: I asked Sahl ibn Hunayf, saying: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say anything about Medina? He said: I heard him say: It is inviolable, safe; it is inviolable, safe."
"5619","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab, with another chain, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us from Yahya al-Himmani, all saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Yusayr ibn Amr, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, gesturing with his hand toward Medina: It is inviolable, safe."
"5620","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Yazid ibn Harun from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Yusayr ibn Amr, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Medina, so he said: An inviolable sanctuary, safe; an inviolable sanctuary, safe."
"5621","Sa'id ibn Dhi Huddan from Sahl ibn Hunayf. Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman from Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida from his father from Abu Ishaq from Sa'id ibn Dhi Huddan, that Sahl ibn Hunayf said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as pilgrims, entering ihram for hajj; when we arrived at Mecca he commanded us to make it umra."
"5622","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, both saying: Abu Kurayb narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Yusuf from his father from Abu Ishaq from Sa'id ibn Dhi Huddan, that Sahl ibn Hunayf used to say: I have never seen the like of one who does not suspect his opinion; we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as pilgrims; when we arrived at Mecca he commanded us to make it umra."
"5623","Al-Rabab from Sahl ibn Hunayf. Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad, with another chain, and Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sufi narrated to us from Ubayd Allah ibn A'isha, with another chain, and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us from Yahya al-Himmani, all saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us from Uthman ibn Hakim from al-Rabab, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: We passed by a stream; I entered it and bathed, then came out feverish. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Command Abu Thabit to seek refuge. I said to him: O my master, are ruqyas proper? He said: No, except for three: the evil eye, fever, and sting."
"5624","Sahl Ibn al-Hanzaliyya al-Ansari, of Banu Haritha; al-Hanzaliyya is said to be his mother, his father's name Afif; he used to reside in Syria, at Damascus. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Hisham ibn Sa'd from Qays ibn Bishr al-Tha'labi, who said: My father was a companion of Abu al-Darda' at Damascus, and informed me that there was a man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ibn al-Hanzaliyya; he was a solitary man, seldom sitting with people - only prayer, and when he finished, only tasbih, tahlil, and takbir until he reached his family. He passed by us one day while we were with Abu al-Darda' and greeted; Abu al-Darda' said to him: A word that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment and it returned; a man came and sat in the sitting in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, and said to a man beside him: Had you seen us when we met the enemy, and so-and-so stabbed so-and-so, saying: Take it, I am the Ghifari youth - what do you think? He said: I see only that he has voided his reward. Another said: I see no harm. They disputed over that until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard and said: Glory be to Allah, there is no harm in being rewarded and praised. He said: Abu al-Darda' rejoiced at that and kept saying: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He kept saying: Yes, until I said, while he raised his head to him: He will surely mount upon his knees. He passed by us another day and greeted; Abu al-Darda' said: A word that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who spends upon horses in the path of Allah is like one stretching his hands with charity, not withholding it. He said: He passed by us another day and greeted; Abu al-Darda' said to him: A word that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What a man Khuraym al-Asadi is, were it not for the length of his forelock and the trailing of his waist-wrapper. That reached Khuraym, so he took a blade, cut his forelock to his ears, and raised his waist-wrapper to mid-calves. He said: Then he passed by us another day and greeted; Abu al-Darda' said to him: A word that benefits us and does not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are coming tomorrow upon your brothers, so set right your state and set right your dress, until you are like a mole among people; Allah does not love foulness nor foul speech."
"5625","Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Abd Allah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from a truthful man of Qinnasrin called Qays ibn Bishr, who said: My father was of the companions of Abu al-Darda', and narrated to me that there was a devout, secluded man of the Ansar there, hardly ever free of worship, called Ibn al-Hanzaliyya; he would pass by Abu al-Darda', stop by him, and Abu al-Darda' would say: Narrate to us a hadith that benefits us and does not harm you. He narrated to him, saying to him one day: A detachment went out, and a man of Banu Ghifar fought in it, struck a mushrik man, then said: Take it, I am the Ghifari. They returned and reported the Ghifari's word; some Muslims said: He voided his reward, others said: No; until that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no harm in being rewarded and praised. Abu al-Darda' rejoiced at it. Ibn al-Hanzaliyya said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us one day: You are coming upon your brothers, so set right your saddles and your dress until you are as a mole among people; for Allah does not love foulness nor foul speech. Ibn al-Hanzaliyya said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who spends upon a horse in the path of Allah is like one stretching his hand with charity, not withholding it."
"5626","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Asad ibn Musa from Ibn Lahi'a from Hisham ibn Sa'd from Qays ibn Bishr from his father, who said: I heard Ibn al-Hanzaliyya say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment; they met the enemy, and a man charged a man of Banu Ghifar, saying: Take them, I am the Ghifari youth. A man said: His reward is void. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: There is no harm in being rewarded and praised."
"5627","Narrated Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi from Abu Tawba al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' from Mu'awiya ibn Sallam from Zayd ibn Sallam, that he heard Abu Sallam say: Abu Kabsha al-Saluli narrated to me from Sahl Ibn al-Hanzaliyya, that they marched with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn, prolonging the march until evening; prayer came due with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a horseman came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I went ahead of you until I climbed such-and-such mountain, and there were Hawazin in their entirety, with their litters, cattle, and sheep, gathered at Hunayn. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: That is the booty of the Muslims tomorrow, Allah willing. Then he said: Who will guard us tonight? Anas ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Mount. So he mounted a horse of his and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Face this pass until you are at its top, and let us not be taken unawares from your side tonight. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to his prayer place and bowed two rak'as, then said: Have you sensed your horseman? A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we have not sensed him. The call for prayer was made, and the Messenger of Allah, while in prayer, kept turning toward the pass; when he finished his prayer and gave salam, he said: Rejoice, your horseman has come. We looked through the trees in the pass, and there he came, until he stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I went until I was at the top of this pass, where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me; in the morning I climbed both passes and looked and saw no one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you dismount tonight? He said: No, except praying or relieving myself. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You have made it obligatory; it does not matter what you do after it."
"5628","Narrated Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Missisi from Muhammad ibn Musaffa from Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid from Ibn Jabir from Rabi'a ibn Yazid, who said: Abu Kabsha al-Saluli came to Damascus, and Abd Allah ibn Amir al-Yahsibi asked him: What brought you? Did you intend to ask the Commander of the Believers Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan? He said: No, by Allah, I ask no one anything after what Sahl Ibn al-Hanzaliyya narrated to me. He said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Uyayna ibn Badr al-Fazari and al-Aqra' ibn Habis al-Tamimi came and asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he called Mu'awiya, may Allah have mercy on him, and ordered him something I do not know what. Mu'awiya came carrying two sheets, cast one sheet to Uyayna - the more forbearing of the two men - who took it and tied it in his turban, and cast the other to al-Aqra' ibn Habis. He said: What is in it? He said: In it is what I was commanded. He said: A bad envoy of his people if I come to them carrying a sheet I do not know what is in it, like the sheet of al-Mutalammis. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was turned toward a man speaking to him; when he heard his words he took the sheet and opened it - a kneeling camel. He said: Where is the owner of this camel? He was sought but not found. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear Allah regarding these beasts; eat them fat and ride them sound. Then he went on until he entered his house, I with him, and he kept saying as if displeased: Whoever asks people out of wealth, only increases coals of Hell. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is sufficiency of wealth? He said: That he knows his family has what lunches them or dinners them."
"5629","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Asad ibn Musa from Marwan ibn Mu'awiya from Bishr ibn Numayr from al-Qasim al-Shami, who said: Sahl Ibn al-Hanzaliyya passed a man praying laxly toward the qibla, and Sahl said: Advance to your prayer place, lest Satan cut your prayer. I narrate to you only what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"5630","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father, may Allah have mercy on him, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us from Yahya ibn Ma'in, both saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Mu'awiya ibn Salih from Sulayman Abu al-Rabi' from al-Qasim, the freedman of Mu'awiya, who said: I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw people gathered and an old man narrating to them; I said: Who is this? They said: Sahl Ibn al-Hanzaliyya. I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever eats meat, let him perform wudu."
"5631","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Hisham ibn Ammar from Yahya ibn Hamza from al-Mut'im ibn al-Miqdam al-San'ani, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, that he said to Ibn al-Hanzaliyya: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Horses have good tied in their forelocks till the Day of Resurrection, and their people are aided over them; whoever ties a horse in the path of Allah, spending upon it is like one stretching his hand with charity, not withholding it."
"5632","Sahl ibn Abi Hathma al-Ansari: he used to reside in Medina. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq, with another chain, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us from al-Humaydi, both from Sufyan ibn Uyayna, from Safwan ibn Sulaym from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays toward a sutra, let him draw near it, lest Satan cut his prayer."
"5633","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi, with another chain, and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us from Abd al-Razzaq, both saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Bushayr ibn Yasar, that he heard Sahl ibn Abi Hathma say: Abd Allah ibn Sahl was found slain in a faqir or well of the wells of Khaybar; his brother Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with his uncles Huwayyisa and Muhayyisa, sons of Mas'ud. Abd al-Rahman went to speak, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The elder, the elder. Muhayyisa spoke, mentioning the killing of Abd Allah ibn Sahl, saying: O Messenger of Allah, we found Abd Allah ibn Sahl slain; the Jews are people of disbelief and treachery, and they killed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then you swear fifty oaths and become entitled to your companion or his blood. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we swear over what we neither attended nor witnessed? He said: Then the Jews clear themselves to you with fifty oaths. They said: How do we accept the oaths of mushrik people? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid the blood money from his own. Sahl said: A young she-camel of them kicked me."
"5634","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Sulayman ibn Harb from Shu'ba from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Mas'ud ibn Niyar say: Sahl ibn Abi Hathma was in a gathering of ours, and narrated to them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to the estimators: Take and leave a third; if you do not leave - or he said: gather - then leave a fourth."
"5635","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Nu'man from Hammad ibn Zayd from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma and Rafi' ibn Khadij, that they both narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Sahl and Muhayyisa ibn Mas'ud came to Khaybar for a need, separated in its palms, and Abd Allah ibn Sahl was killed. His brother Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with his cousins Muhayyisa and Huwayyisa, sons of Mas'ud. Abd al-Rahman began and spoke, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Honor the elder - saying: The eldest begins speech - and Abd al-Rahman was older than his two companions; they spoke about the killing of their companion. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Become entitled to your slain or your companion with fifty oaths of them. They said: Disbelieving people. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money. Sahl said: I caught a she-camel of those camels, and it kicked me a kick in a sheepfold of theirs."
"5636","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Allan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghamma, both saying: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us from Qays from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, who said: A group of the Ansar went out, and a man of them was killed; that was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Your proof? They said: We have no proof. He said: Then their oaths? They said: Then the Jews would kill us, then swear. He said: Then your oaths. They said: We did not witness. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money."
"5637","Narrated Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti from Abu Nu'aym from Sa'id ibn Ubayd al-Ta'i from Bushayr ibn Yasar, that a man of the Ansar called Sahl ibn Abi Hathma informed him that a group of his people set out for Khaybar, separated in it, and found one of them slain. They said to those among whom they found him: Did you kill our companion? They said: We neither killed him nor knew. So they set out to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, we set out for Khaybar and found one of us slain. The youngest of the people spoke, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The elder, the elder. He said to them: You bring proof against the killer. They said: We have no proof. He said: Then they swear to you. They said: We do not accept the oaths of the Jews. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that his blood be voided, so he paid his blood money with a hundred camels of sadaqa."
"5638","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qa'nabi from Malik, with another chain, and Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Malik, from Abu Layla ibn Abd Allah ibn Sahl, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, that he informed him, from elder men of his people, that Abd Allah ibn Sahl and Muhayyisa went out to Khaybar out of hardship that befell them. Muhayyisa was brought and informed that Abd Allah ibn Sahl had been killed and thrown in a faqir or spring. He went to the Jews and said: By Allah, you killed him. They said: By Allah, we did not kill him. Then he returned until he came to his people and mentioned that to them. He, his brother Huwayyisa - older than him - and Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl came; Huwayyisa went to speak - he was the one at Khaybar - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muhayyisa: Honor age - meaning seniority - then Huwayyisa spoke, then Muhayyisa spoke. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Either they pay the blood money of your companion, or they permit war. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to them of that, and they wrote: By Allah, we did not kill him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Huwayyisa, Muhayyisa, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl: Will you swear and become entitled to the blood of your companion? They said: No. He said: Then the Jews swear to you? They said: They are not Muslims. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money from his own, sending them a hundred she-camels, until they were brought into their house. Sahl said: A red she-camel of them kicked me."
"5639","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yahya from Shu'ba from Yahya ibn Sa'id from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Salih ibn Khawwat, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, regarding the fear prayer, who said: The imam stands facing the qibla, and a group of them stands toward the enemy, their faces to the enemy; he prays with those with him one rak'a, then stands, and they bow for themselves one rak'a and prostrate two prostrations in their place; then these go to the station of those, and those come; he bows with them one rak'a - it is two for him and one for them - then they bow for themselves and prostrate two prostrations."
"5640","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yahya from Shu'ba from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Salih ibn Khawwat, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5641","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi, with another chain, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, from Sufyan ibn Uyayna from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling dates for dates, and permitted araya to be sold by their estimate, their owners eating them fresh."
"5642","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Asad ibn Musa from Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida from Sufyan from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided Khaybar into halves: a half for his needs and his special share, and a half among the Muslims; he divided it among them over eighteen shares."
"5643","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father, with another chain, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, both saying: Abu Usama narrated to us from al-Walid ibn Kathir, who said: Bushayr ibn Yasar, freedman of Banu Haritha, narrated to me that Rafi' ibn Khadij and Sahl ibn Abi Hathma narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabana - muzabana is dates for dates - except the owners of araya, for he permitted them."
"5644","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rishdin from Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from Ibn Lahi'a from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the minbar: Avoid the seven enormities. People fell silent and no one spoke, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not ask me about them? Polytheism with Allah, killing a soul, fleeing from battle, consuming the orphan's wealth, consuming riba, slandering a chaste woman, and returning to bedouin life after hijra."
"5645","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays from Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr, and al-Hajjaj from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathma, from his uncle Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, both saying: Habiba bint Sahl was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas al-Ansari; she disliked him, and he was an ugly man. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I see him; were it not for fear of Allah, mighty and majestic, I would spit in his face. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you return to him his garden which he gave you as dowry? I said: Yes. So he sent to him, and she returned his garden to him, and he separated them; that was the first khul' in Islam."
"5646","Sahl Abu Iyas al-Ansari then al-Sa'idi. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam, who said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Madani narrated to me from Abu Hazim, that he sat beside Iyas ibn Sahl al-Ansari of Banu Sa'ida in their mosque, and he said: Turn to what you turned to, O Abu Hazim; shall I not narrate to you from my father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: That I pray fajr, then sit in a sitting remembering Allah, mighty and majestic, until the sun rises, is dearer to me than charging upon fine horses in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"5647","Sahl ibn Haritha al-Ansari: he used to reside in Medina. Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd from Anas ibn Iyad from Sa'd ibn Sa'd ibn Ujra, from Sahl ibn Haritha al-Ansari, who said: A people complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they settled a house while numerous, then died out. He said: Why did you not leave it, for it is blameworthy?"
"5648","Sahl ibn Malik, nephew of Ka'b: he used to reside in Medina. Narrated Ali ibn Ishaq al-Wazir al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami from Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Sinan ibn Malik ibn Misma', from Sahl ibn Yusuf ibn Sahl, nephew of Ka'b, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina from the Farewell Hajj, he ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, Abu Bakr never wronged me at all; recognize that for him. O people, I am pleased with Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and the first Muhajirun; being pleased, recognize that for them. O people, preserve me in my companions, my in-laws, and my brothers-in-law; let Allah not seek you for the wrong of any of them. O people, remove what is disapproved from the Muslims, and when one of them dies, speak good of him."
"5649","Sahl ibn Sakhr - also said Suhayl, the correct is Sahl: he used to reside in Basra. Narrated Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Aswad from Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti, with another chain, and Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us from Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti from his father, from his grandfather, who said: Suhayl ibn Sakhr, who had companionship, said to me: When I own the price of a slave, I buy a slave with it, for fortunes are in the forelocks of men."
"5650","Sahl ibn Qays al-Ansari: a participant at Badr, martyred on the day of Uhud. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who attended Badr, then of Banu Jusham ibn al-Khazraj: Sahl ibn Qays Abi al-Qayn ibn Ka'b ibn Sawwad ibn Ghanm ibn Ka'b ibn Salama."
"5651","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who attended Badr, of Banu Sawwad ibn Ghanm: Sahl ibn Qays ibn Abi Ka'b ibn al-Qayn."
"5652","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of Uhud, then of Banu Sawwad: Sahl ibn Qays ibn Abi Ka'b ibn al-Qayn."
"5653","Sahl ibn Adi al-Ansari: a participant at Badr. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who attended Badr, then of Banu Mu'awiya ibn Awf ibn al-Khazraj: Sahl ibn Adi."
"5654","Sahl ibn Amir al-Ansari: martyred on the day of Bi'r Ma'una. Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Ibn Lahi'a from Abu al-Aswad from Urwa, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of Bi'r Ma'una, then of Banu al-Najjar: Sahl ibn Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Amr ibn Thaqif."
"5655","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi from Muhammad ibn Fulayh from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those of the Ansar martyred on the day of Bi'r Ma'una, then of Banu al-Najjar: Sahl ibn Amir ibn Sa'd."
"5656","589 - Sahl ibn Adi al-Tamimi, an ally of the Ansar, martyred on the day of Yamama. 5648 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those martyred on the day of Yamama from the Ansar, then from Banu Abd al-Ashhal: Sahl ibn Adi of Banu Tamim, an ally of theirs."
"5657","590 - Sahl ibn Atik, an Aqabi. 5649 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, regarding the naming of those who attended al-Aqaba to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Sahl ibn Atik."
"5658","591 - Sahl al-Balawi, the man of the two sa's, an Ansari who used to reside in Madina. 5650 - Narrated Musa ibn Harun, Umar ibn Zurara al-Hadathi narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, Said ibn Uthman al-Balawi narrated, from his grandmother the daughter of Adi, that her mother Umayra bint Sahl, the man of the two sa's whom the hypocrites mocked, narrated to her that he went out with his zakat, a sa' of dates, along with his daughter Umayra, until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and poured it out, then said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a request of you. He said: And what is it? He said: That you invoke Allah for blessing for me and for her, and wipe her head, for I have no child besides her. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand on me, and I swear by Allah, it was as if the coolness of the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon my liver."
"5659","592 - Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi; mention of the age of Sahl ibn Sa'd and his death. 5651 - Narrated Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Sahl ibn Sa'd, kunya Abu al-Abbas, died in Madina in the year ninety-one, at the age of ninety-six."
"5660","5652 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, he said: Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi died in the year ninety-one."
"5661","5653 - Narrated Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamza informed, from al-Zuhri, he said: Sahl ibn Sa'd said, and he had seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard from him, and he mentioned that he was fifteen years old on the day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away."
"5662","5654 - Narrated Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Sahl ibn Sa'd said, and he had seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard from him, that he was fifteen years old on the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away."
"5663","5655 - Narrated Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Ansari said, and he had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was fifteen years old in his time."
"5664","5656 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated, Abd al-Hamid narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he was in a gathering of his people narrating to them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while some of them were turned toward others chatting, so he became angry, then said: Look at them; I narrate to them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of what my eyes saw and my ears heard, while some of them are turned toward others. By Allah, I shall surely leave from among you, then never return to you again. I said to him: Where are you going? He said: I am going to strive in the path of Allah. I said: You are in no condition for jihad; you cannot hold onto a horse, you cannot strike with a sword, and you cannot thrust with a spear. He said: O Abu Hazim, I shall go and stand in the ranks, then a passerby or a stone will strike me among them, and Allah will grant me martyrdom. He said: So he went, by my life, and he did not return except pierced."
"5665","5657 - Narrated Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he married seventy women in wedlock, and they either died or he separated from them, and he saw nothing wrong in that."
"5666","And from what Sahl ibn Sa'd transmitted with isnad: Abu Hurayra from Sahl ibn Sa'd. 5658 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf al-Tustari, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you brandish a sword against his brother, for perhaps Satan may snatch at his hand and he falls into a pit of the pits of Hellfire."
"5667","Said ibn al-Musayyib from Sahl ibn Sa'd. 5659 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated, Abu al-Ghusn Thabit ibn Qays narrated, that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyib narrating from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he attended the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marrying a man in return for two surahs which he would teach from the Qur'an."
"5668","What al-Zuhri narrated from Sahl ibn Sa'd, a chapter. 5660 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that a man peeked at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through the curtain of the chamber, while in the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was an iron comb. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I known this one was waiting for me until I came to him, I would have stabbed him in his eyes with the comb. And was seeking permission instituted except on account of sight?"
"5669","5661 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, al-Awza'i narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he informed him that a man peeked at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the chamber, while in the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was an iron comb. He said: Had I known this one was waiting for me until I came to him, I would have stabbed him in his eyes with the comb. And was seeking permission instituted except on account of sight?"
"5670","5662 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated, from al-Layth ibn Sa'd; and narrated Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Ibn Shihab narrated to me that Sahl ibn Sa'd, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that a man peeked through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he said: Had I known you were waiting for me, I would have stabbed you in your eye with it. Seeking permission was only instituted on account of sight."
"5671","5663 - Narrated Bishr ibn Musa, al-Humaydi narrated; and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated, both said: Sufyan narrated, al-Zuhri narrated, he said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd saying: A man peeked from the chamber of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. He said: Had I known you were waiting for me, I would have stabbed you in your eye with it. Seeking permission was only instituted on account of sight."
"5672","5664 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, my uncle narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"5673","5665 - Narrated Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that a man peeked through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was scratching his head with an iron comb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I known you were waiting for me, I would have stabbed you in your eye with it. Seeking permission was only instituted on account of sight."
"5674","5666 - Narrated Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi informed him that a man peeked through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was combing, or scratching, his head. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I known you were waiting for me, I would have stabbed you in your eye with it. Permission was only instituted on account of sight."
"5675","5667 - Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated, Khalid informed, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he informed him that a man peeked through a hole in the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I known you were waiting for me, I would have stabbed you in your eye with it. The screen was only made for permission, or he said: on account of looking."
"5676","5668 - Narrated al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani, both said: Isa ibn Uthman al-Kisa'i narrated, Yahya ibn Isa narrated, from Sufyan, from Abu Salama, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in his chamber with an iron comb, combing his beard with it, a person came and peeked through a hole in his chamber. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him and said: Had I known you were waiting for me, I would have gouged your eye with this comb. Permission was only instituted on account of sight. This Abu Salama from whom Sufyan narrated is Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah."
"5677","5669 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Abu Dawud narrated, Zam'a ibn Salih narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that a man peeked through a hole at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. He said: Had I known you were looking, I would have stood until I stabbed you in your eye with it. Permission was only instituted on account of sight."
"5678","5670 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri, Zakariyya ibn Yahya, scribe of al-Umari, narrated, Rushdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: A man peeked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a stick or an iron comb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I known you were looking at me, I would have gouged your eye."
"5679","5671 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Bazzaz, Abu Khaythama Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, my father narrated to me, from Salih, from Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, that Sahl ibn Sa'd informed him that a man peeked through a hole in the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, he said: Had I known you were looking at me, I would have stabbed you in your eye with it. Seeking permission was only instituted on account of sight."
"5680","5672 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqa, Ismail ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated, from Umar ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a man gazing into his house, while in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was an iron comb with which he was combing his head. He said: Had I known you were looking at me, I would have stabbed you in your eye with it."
"5681","5673 - Narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri, Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli narrated, Salama ibn Rawh narrated, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi informed me that a man peeked through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was combing his head. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Had I known you were looking at me, I would have stabbed you in your eye with it. Permission was only instituted on account of looking."
"5682","A chapter. 5674 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ibn Jurayj informed, Ibn Shihab informed me, regarding li'an and the sunna concerning it, from the hadith of Sahl ibn Sa'd, brother of Banu Sa'ida, that a man of the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife; should he kill him and then you kill him, or what should he do? So Allah revealed concerning his case what is mentioned in the Qur'an of the matter of the two invoking li'an. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Allah has decreed regarding you and your wife. He said: So they invoked li'an in the mosque while I was a witness. When they finished, he said: I have lied against her, O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her. So he divorced her thrice before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him, when they finished the li'an. So he separated from her in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is the separation between every two invoking li'an. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If she bears him reddish, short, as if a wahara, then I consider her truthful and him lying against her; and if she bears him black, large-eyed, with large buttocks, then I consider him truthful against her. So she bore him of the disliked description thereof."
"5683","5675 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik; and narrated Bakr ibn Sahl, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Malik informed, from Ibn Shihab, that Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi informed him that Uwaymir ibn Ashqar al-Ajlani came to Asim ibn Adi al-Ansari and said to him: O Asim, what do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife; should he kill him and then you kill him, or what should he do? Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that for me, O Asim. So Asim asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he disliked such questions and censured them, until what Asim had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weighed heavily upon Asim. When Asim returned to his family, Uwaymir came to him and said: O Asim, what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to you? Asim said to Uwaymir: You have never brought me any good; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked the question you asked him about. Uwaymir said: By Allah, I shall not stop until I ask him about it. So Uwaymir came until he reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was among the people and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife; should he kill him and then you kill him, or what should he do? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has been revealed concerning you and your companion, so go and bring her. Sahl said: So they invoked li'an while I was with the people in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they finished, Uwaymir said: I have lied against her if I keep her. So Uwaymir divorced her thrice before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him. Ibn Shihab said: So it became the sunna of the two invoking li'an."
"5684","5676 - Narrated Abu Khalifa, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma' narrated, Juwayriya ibn Asma' narrated, from Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, that Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi informed him that Uwaymir of Banu al-Ajlan came to Asim ibn Adi and said: O Asim, what do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife; should he kill him and then you kill him, or what should he do? So ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that for me, O Asim. Then he mentioned the like thereof."
"5685","5677 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, al-Awza'i narrated, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that Uwaymir came to Asim ibn Adi, who was the chief of Banu al-Ajlan, and said: What do you say of a man who finds another man with his wife; should he kill him and then you kill him, or what should he do? And he said: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that for me. So Asim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man finds another man with his wife; should he kill him and then you kill him, or what should he do? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked such questions. Then Uwaymir asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked such questions and censured them. Uwaymir said: By Allah, I shall not stop until I ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that. He said: So Uwaymir came and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man finds another man with his wife; should he kill him and then you kill him, or what should he do? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qur'an has been revealed concerning you and your companion. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them both with mula'ana as Allah explained it in His Book. So they invoked li'an. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her I have wronged her. He said: Then he divorced her, and it became a sunna for those after them of the two invoking li'an. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch her; if she bears him dark, intensely black-eyed, large-buttocked, thick-shanked, then I consider Uwaymir truthful against her; and if she bears him reddish, as if a wahara, then I consider Uwaymir lying against her. He said: So she bore him of the description the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described as proof of Uwaymir's truthfulness, and this child's lineage was traced to his mother."
"5686","5678 - Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi, both said: Asim ibn Ali narrated, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that Uwaymir came to Asim ibn Adi and said: What do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife, then kills him so you kill him for it? Ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me, O Asim. So Asim came and asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who disliked such questions and censured them. He returned and told him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had disliked such questions and censured them. Uwaymir said: By Allah, I shall surely come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he came, while the Qur'an had already been revealed after Asim left. He asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A Qur'an has been revealed concerning you two. So he called them both, they stepped forward and invoked li'an. Then he said: I have lied against her, O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her, so he separated from her, though the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not command him to separate. So it became the sunna of the two invoking li'an. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch; if she bears him red, short, like a wahara, then I consider him lying against her; and if she bears him dark, large-eyed, with buttocks, then I consider him truthful against her. So she bore him of the disliked description."
"5687","5679 - Narrated Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he said: A man of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife; should he kill him? So Allah revealed concerning his case what is mentioned in the Qur'an of li'an. He said: It has been decreed concerning you and your wife. He said: So they invoked li'an while I was a witness. Then he separated from her in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it became the sunna thereafter concerning them that the two invoking li'an be separated. She was pregnant and he denied her pregnancy, so her son was attributed to his mother. Then the sunna continued in inheritance, that her son inherits from her and she inherits from him what is apportioned for her."
"5688","5680 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Numayr al-Misri, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from Uqayl and Rushdin ibn Sa'd, from Uqayl and Qurra ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Shihab, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that a man of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife; then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Abu Salih, from al-Layth, from Uqayl."
"5689","5681 - Narrated Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, that Ibn Shihab wrote mentioning that Sahl ibn Sa'd informed him that Uwaymir said to his cousin Asim ibn Adi: Come with us to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What do you think, if I found another man with my wife, should I kill him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked his statement, so he returned, and Uwaymir said: I shall surely mention that to him even if he dislikes it. So Uwaymir came to him and said: What do you think, if I find another man with my wife? He said: Bring your wife, for it has come down concerning you two. So he brought her and they invoked li'an. Then he said: I have fabricated against her, so he separated between them. Ibn Shihab said: So it became a sunna among the Muslims, his separating from her."
"5690","5682 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated; and narrated Bishr ibn Musa, al-Humaydi narrated, both said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he informed him, he said: Uwaymir al-Ajlani came to Asim ibn Adi and said: O Asim, ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me about a man who finds another man with his wife and kills him; will he be killed for him, or what should he do? So Asim asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, who censured such questions and disliked it. Then Uwaymir came and said: O Asim, what did you do? He said: What did I do? You have brought me no good; I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he censured such questions. Uwaymir said: By Allah, I shall surely come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him. So he came to him and found that revelation had come down concerning them both. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them both and made li'an between them. Uwaymir said: If I take her back I have surely lied against her, so he separated from her before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him. Ibn Shihab said: So it became the sunna of the two invoking li'an. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch her; if she bears him dark, intensely black-eyed, large-buttocked, then I consider him truthful against her; and if she bears him reddish, as if a wahara, then I consider him a liar. So she bore him of the disliked description. And the wording is that of the hadith of al-Humaydi."
"5691","5683 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anbar al-Basri, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who sees another man with his wife; should he kill him so you kill him for him, or what should he do with him? So Allah revealed concerning them both what is mentioned in the Qur'an of li'an. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: It has been decreed concerning you and your wife. He said: So they invoked li'an while I was a witness in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her I have lied against her, so he separated from her. So the sunna continued thereafter concerning them that the two invoking li'an be separated. She was pregnant and he denied her pregnancy, and the child was attributed to her. And the sunna continued thereafter in inheritance, that he inherits from her, and she inherits from him what Allah apportioned for her."
"5692","5684 - Narrated Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Iyad ibn Abd Allah al-Fihri informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that the man invoking li'an divorced her with three divorces in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) executed it; and what was done in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a sunna. Sahl said: I attended this in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the sunna continued thereafter concerning the two invoking li'an that they be separated, then never reunite ever. Ibn Shihab said: And the man said at that time: What an evil servant of Allah I am, if I lied in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and bore a slander."
"5693","5685 - Narrated Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, he said: I attended their li'an in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was fifteen years old. When they finished their mutual invocation he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have lied against her if I keep her. He said: So he divorced her thrice. And he said: By Allah, if I lied I have surely borne a slander. Then she passed by pregnant, and the child was attributed to his mother."
"5694","5686 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Fudayl al-Malti, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi' narrated; and narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, meaning Ibn Mujammi', from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: Uwaymir, a man of the Ansar of Banu al-Ajlan, came to Asim ibn Adi and said: Ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife and kills him; will you kill him, or what should he do? The man waited a while, then came and said: O Asim, what did you do about what I told you? Asim said: You have never brought me any good; I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he censured such questions. His soul gave him no rest until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him the same as he had said to Asim. He said: Come, for Allah has revealed concerning you and your companion. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them both and made li'an between them. Uwaymir said: O Prophet of Allah, I have lied against her if I keep her after invoking li'an with her. So the sunna continued between the two invoking li'an that they be separated."
"5695","5687 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he attended the two invoking li'an, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between them."
"5696","5688 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Abu Amir al-Nahwi, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Ja'far ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: Uwaymir said to Asim: A man finds another man with his wife; should he kill him so you kill him, or what should he do? Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that for me. So Asim asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, who disliked such questions and censured them. That weighed heavily upon Asim and grew grave in his soul. Then Uwaymir came to him and said: Did you ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I commanded you with? He said: You have brought me no good; I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he disliked such questions and censured them, until I wished I had forfeited my wealth rather than ask him your matter concerning your wife. So Uwaymir came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man finds another man with his wife; should he kill him so you kill him, or what should he do? He said: Allah has revealed concerning you and your companion, so hasten with her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) presented her in the mosque after Asr while I was with the people watching. So they invoked li'an. When they finished, Uwaymir stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wronged her if I keep her; she is divorced irrevocably."
"5697","5689 - Narrated Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that when Uwaymir invoked li'an with his wife in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Uwaymir stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wronged her if I keep her; she is divorced irrevocably."
"5698","5690 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Abu Dawud narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama and Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that Asim ibn Adi said: Uwaymir, a man of Banu al-Ajlan, came, then he mentioned the hadith, like the hadith of Ibrahim ibn Sa'd."
"5699","5691 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated, from al-Zuhri, who heard Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he witnessed the two invoking li'an at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they were separated. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have lied against her if I keep her."
"5700","5692 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama al-Majishun narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: A man of Banu al-Ajlan came to Asim ibn Adi and said: O Asim, what do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife; should he kill him so you kill him, or what should he do? Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked such questions and censured them, until what he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weighed heavily upon Asim. When Asim returned to his family, Uwaymir came and said: O Asim, what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to you? Asim said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked the question you asked about. So Uwaymir came until he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) amid the people. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife; should he kill him so you kill him, or what should he do? He said: It has come down concerning you and your companion, so go and bring her. Sahl said: So they invoked li'an while I was with the people in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they finished their mutual invocation, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have lied against her if I keep her. He said: So he divorced her before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to divorce her; and his separating from her became a sunna between the two invoking li'an."
"5701","A chapter. 5693 - Narrated Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Khunays al-Dimyati, Musa ibn Muhammad al-Balqawi narrated, al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muqri narrated, from al-Zuhri, Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to Banu Amr ibn Awf to reconcile between them. The time of prayer came, so the mu'adhdhin came to Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, and said: Will you lead the people in prayer? He said: Yes. So Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, prayed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while the people were in prayer, and he slipped through until he stood in the row with the people. Abu Bakr would not turn in his prayer. When the people clapped much, he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to remain in your place. So Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, raised his hand and praised Allah for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had commanded him of that. Then he stepped back until he stood straight in the row. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed. When he finished he said: O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from staying firm when I commanded you? Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, said: It would not befit Ibn Abi Quhafa to pray before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did I see you clap so much? Whoever is beset by something in prayer, let him glorify Allah; for when he glorifies, he is attended to; and clapping is only for women."
"5702","5694 - Narrated Mas'ada ibn Sa'd al-Attar al-Makki and Ahmad ibn Anbar al-Misri, both said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated, from Musa ibn Uqba, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud: O Allah, forgive my people, for they do not know."
"5703","5695 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only permitted us mut'a on account of a dire need of the people, then he forbade it afterwards."
"5704","5696 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The statement of the Ansar used to be, water is from water, at the beginning of Islam; then ghusl came afterwards."
"5705","Al-Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd from his father. 5697 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Atiq ibn Ya'qub al-Zubayri narrated, Ubayy ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about cleaning oneself after relieving oneself. He said: Can none of you find three stones? Two stones for the two sides, and a stone for the outlet."
"5706","5698 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Duhaym, my father narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no wudu for one who does not invoke blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5707","5699 - Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiya al-Utbi al-Misri, Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadari narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Ubayy ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer for one who has no wudu; and no wudu for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it; and no prayer for one who does not invoke blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and no prayer for one who does not love the Ansar."
"5708","5700 - Narrated Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Ma'n ibn Isa narrated, from Ubayy ibn Abbas ibn Sahl, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a horse in a garden called al-Luhayf."
"5709","5701 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had every night a tray from Sa'd ibn Ubada. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to propose to women, saying: For you is such-and-such, and the bowl of Sa'd goes with me to you wherever I go."
"5710","5702 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deliberation is from Allah, and haste is from Satan."
"5711","5703 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give one salutation to his right."
"5712","5704 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) blessed the well of Buda'a and spat in it."
"5713","5705 - Narrated al-Husayn, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl narrated, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: His name was Hazn, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Sahl."
"5714","5706 - And with its isnad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and never occurred to the heart of anyone."
"5715","5707 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no ill omen; and if there be ill omen in anything, it is in the horse, the woman, and the dwelling."
"5716","5708 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, Ali ibn Bahr narrated; and narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Abu Mus'ab narrated, both said: Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking by bending the mouths of waterskins."
"5717","5709 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love Quraysh, for whoever loves them, Allah Almighty loves him."
"5718","5710 - And from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Renew Islam through love of the Ansar, for none loves them but a believer, and none hates them but a hypocrite."
"5719","5711 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I was indeed present on the day of Uhud, and I was looking when the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was struck and wounded. I know who was washing the blood from the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and who was carrying water in a shield. The wound refused to stop bleeding, until Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), burned a worn mat and placed its ash upon it, and it stopped. The one carrying water in the shield was Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and Fatima was the one washing the blood and treating it."
"5720","5712 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon Dhubab. Abu al-Qasim said: I was informed that Dhubab is a mountain in the Hijaz, and his saying he prayed upon it means he blessed it."
"5721","5713 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, Abu al-Rabi' al-Harithi narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon Dhubab."
"5722","5714 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr, Abu al-Rabi' narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: We used to rejoice at Friday. An old woman of us would send to Quda'a, take some beet leaves, then sprinkle over them a handful of barley and cook it, then serve it to us, and we would lick it. So we rejoiced at Friday on account of that."
"5723","5715 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr, Abu al-Rabi' al-Harithi narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to al-Aliya, then catch Maghrib at the camel resting-place, and they would perform tayammum."
"5724","5716 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl narrated, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"5725","5717 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Abu Mus'ab narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that he attended the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud."
"5726","5718 - And with its isnad, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted a share by arrow to Sa'd ibn Sa'd on the day of Badr, and he is the brother of Sahl ibn Sa'd."
"5727","5719 - And with its isnad, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined doing good to our doers of good, and overlooking our offenders."
"5728","5720 - Narrated Musa ibn Harun, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated; and narrated Abdan, Abu Mus'ab narrated, both said: Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Tabuk, while upon the mountain pass, he said: Allah is Greatest. When he looked at Uhud he said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. Then he turned and said: Would you like me to inform you of the quarters of the Ansar? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best quarters of the Ansar are Abd al-Ashhal, then the abode of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj, then the abode of Banu al-Najjar, then the abode of Banu Sa'ida. Sa'd said to him: O Messenger of Allah, have you made us the last of the tribes? He said: If you are of the best, that suffices you. And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu Mus'ab."
"5729","5721 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, Ali ibn Bahr narrated; and narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Abu Mus'ab narrated, both said: Abd al-Muhaymin narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rinse your mouths from milk, for it has greasiness."
"5730","5722 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Abu Mus'ab narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing into drink, and drinking from the broken edge of the cup or its handle."
"5731","5723 - And with its isnad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command wiping over the two leather socks."
"5732","5724 - Narrated Abdan, Abu Mus'ab narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that Amir ibn al-Tufayl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madina. He disputed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and raised his voice, while Thabit ibn Qays stood with his sword over the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Amir, lower your voice before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What are you to that? Thabit said: By the One who honored him, were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would dislike it, I would strike your head with this sword. Amir looked at him while seated and Thabit standing, and said to him: By Allah, O Thabit, if your soul were exposed to me you would surely turn away from me. Thabit said: By Allah, O Amir, if your soul were exposed to my tongue you would surely detest your life. Then a nephew of Amir sneezed and praised Allah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked mercy upon him. Then Amir sneezed but did not praise Allah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not invoke mercy upon him. Amir said: You invoked mercy upon this boy and left me? He said: He praised Allah. He said: Then by his oath, I shall surely fill it against you with horses and men. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah suffices me against you, and the two sons of Qayla. Then Amir left and gathered against the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Three clans of Banu Sulaym joined him, those whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to invoke against: Usayya, Dhakwan, and Ri'l. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to invoke against them in the dawn prayer: O Allah, curse Lihyan, Ri'l, Dhakwan, and Usayya, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger; Allah is Greatest. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for seventeen nights. When he heard that Amir had gathered against him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent among them Amr ibn Umayya al-Damri and the rest of them from the Ansar, their commander al-Mundhir ibn Amr. They went until they alighted at Bi'r Ma'una. Then he advanced until he fell upon them and killed them all; none escaped of them except Amr ibn Umayya, who was among the mounts. Allah revealed to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day they were killed the news of his Companions, and he said: Your Companions have been killed, so consider your opinion. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against Amir, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, suffice me against Amir. So Allah sufficed him against him. He came until he alighted in his courtyard, then Allah struck him with a throat abscess in his throat in the house of a woman of Salul. He began leaping while saying: O woe to Amir, from a gland like a camel's gland, in the house of a Saluliyya woman, hoping to die in her house. He remained thus until he died in her house. Arbad ibn Qays was struck by a thunderbolt and burned, and he died. And those with them returned."
"5733","5725 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, Abu Mus'ab narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin narrated, from his grandfather, that he pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he and Abu Dharr, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, Muhammad ibn Maslama, and another man, upon that the blame of no blamer would seize them regarding Allah."
"5734","5726 - Narrated Musa ibn Harun, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, he said: Before he built the mosque, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray toward a wooden post. When he built the mosque, a mihrab was built for him, so he stepped forward to it, and the wooden post moaned like a camel's moan. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand upon it and it fell silent."
"5735","5727 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that he carried a step of the minbar's steps from al-Ghaba until he placed it in the mosque, and that the wood of the minbar was of tamarisk."
"5736","5728 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani, Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, the shrike, and the frog."
"5737","5729 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, Abu al-Rabi' al-Harithi narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had with my father three horses which he would feed. He said: And I heard my father naming them: al-Ladan, al-Lahif, and al-Tarab."
"5738","5730 - And with its isnad, he said: On the day of Khaybar, while we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he took the banner and said: I shall give this banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger. The people craned to see to whom he would give it. So he called Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, while Ali had ophthalmia. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in his eyes, then gave it to him, and Allah granted victory upon his hands."
"5739","5731 - And with its isnad, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O people, fear Allah, for if you fear Allah, Allah will soon satiate you with the oil of Sham and the wheat of Sham."
"5740","5732 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated, Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Umari narrated, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lean upon a trunk. When the people grew many he said: The people have grown many; if only there were a minbar upon which I could sit. Abbas said: So my father went and cut the minbar's wood from al-Ghaba; I do not know whether he made it or had it made."
"5741","5733 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi' narrated, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Aslami narrated, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl, from his father Sahl, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Khandaq. He took the pickaxe and dug with it, and struck a rock, and laughed. It was said: What makes you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I laughed at people who will come to you from the east, driven to Paradise while unwilling."
"5742","5734 - Narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, al-Abbas ibn Sahl informed me, from his father, he said: When we invoked li'an, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep her with you until she gives birth; if she bears him red like a wahara, then he belongs to his father Uwaymir, who disowned him; and if she bears him black of tongue and hair, then he belongs to Ibn al-Sahma', the man accused with her. Uwaymir said: When she gave birth to him, I came to him; he faced me like a black fur, then I took his two cheeks and his tongue faced me like a date. So I said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth."
"5743","5735 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated, Abd al-Hakim ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwa narrated, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to relieve himself, let him neither face the qibla nor turn his back to it."
"5744","5736 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi and Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj, both said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'a narrated, from Umara ibn Ghaziyya, he said: I heard al-Abbas ibn Sahl narrating from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The best tribes of the Ansar are the quarters of Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith, then Banu Sa'ida; and in all the Ansar there is good."
"5745","5737 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, Hazim ibn Tammam narrated to me, from Abbas ibn Sahl al-Ansari then al-Sa'idi, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I pray Fajr, then sit in my place and remember Allah until the sun rises, is dearer to me than riding out upon fine horses in the path of Allah. Thus al-Dabari said: Ayyash; though it is Abbas."
"5746","5738 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi al-Basri, Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated, my father narrated to me, Abu Khaythama narrated, al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr narrated, Isa ibn Abd Allah ibn Malik narrated, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, one of Banu Malik, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl al-Sa'idi, that he was in a gathering in which were his father, Abu Hurayra, Abu Usayd, and Abu Humayd, and that they recalled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they mentioned that he gave salutation to his right and to his left."
"5747","What Abu Hazim Salama ibn Dinar narrated from Sahl ibn Sa'd: narration of the Madinans from Abu Hazim; Ubayd Allah ibn Umar from Abu Hazim from Sahl. 5739 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father narrated to me, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd - Hammad said: Then I met Abu Hazim and he narrated it to me, and I denied nothing of what he narrated to me - then he mentioned the hadith of prayer. He said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: It would not befit Ibn Abi Quhafa to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer. Then he said: When something befalls you in prayer, let the men glorify Allah, and let the women clap."
"5748","Umara ibn Ghaziyya from Abu Hazim. 5740 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Asim ibn Ali narrated; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, both said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Umara ibn Ghaziyya, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no believer who calls talbiya but whatever is to his right and to his left, of tree or stone, calls with him, until the earth ends from here and here. The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those below them as a star is seen in the sky."
"5749","5741 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, from Mu'awiya ibn Salih, from Umara ibn Ghaziyya, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no one calling talbiya who calls but whatever is to his right and left, of stone and tree, calls with him."
"5750","Muhammad ibn Ajlan from Abu Hazim. 5742 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Missisi, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' al-Burani narrated, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was summoned for help regarding Banu Amr ibn Awf over a matter between them, to reconcile it. Prayer was established and they waited; when he was delayed, Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stepped forward. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and the people clapped to Abu Bakr to step back. So Abu Bakr stepped back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he turned to the people and said: What is this clapping? Glorification is for men, and clapping is for women."
"5751","Mus'ab ibn Thabit ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr from Abu Hazim. 5743 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Marwazi narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Mus'ab ibn Thabit informed, Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Sahl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The believer, among the people of faith, is like the head in relation to the body; the believer aches for the people of faith as the body aches for what is in the head."
"5752","5744 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated; and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Ahmad ibn Janab al-Missisi narrated, both said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim Salama ibn Dinar, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is affectionate, and there is no good in one who neither shows affection nor is shown affection."
"5753","5745 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari, Mu'ammal ibn Ihab narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Walid al-Adani narrated, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise, and lo, a sound; I looked, and lo, it was Bilal."
"5754","5746 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Nadr, Mu'ammal ibn Ihab narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Walid al-Adani narrated, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say: There is no god but Allah, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"5755","Hisham ibn Sa'd from Abu Hazim. 5747 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated, from Abu Hazim, he said: Ill omen was mentioned to Sahl ibn Sa'd, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: If it be in anything, it is in the woman, the dwelling, and the horse."
"5756","5748 - Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"5757","5749 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Banu Amr ibn Awf to reconcile between them over a matter they differed in. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not arrive until the noon prayer was established, and Abu Bakr stepped forward to lead the people in prayer and uttered the takbir. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered; the people saw him and began clapping to Abu Bakr, to alert him to the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, would not turn in his prayer. When he heard the parting of the rows behind him, he knew the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had come, so he stepped back to the row. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand between the shoulders of Abu Bakr until he brought him forward to his station, but Abu Bakr remained a little, then drew back in one movement and entered the row. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed for them until he finished the prayer. Then he gave salutation and turned to Abu Bakr and said: What prompted you, O Abu Bakr, to do what you did; why did you not stay firm when I brought you forward? He said: I had intended that, but I did not consider it fitting for Ibn Abi Quhafa to step forward before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he turned to the people and said: When a contingency befalls you, upon you is glorification; for glorification is for men, and clapping is for women."
"5758","5750 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, that he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a woman came to him and said: I have come, O Messenger of Allah, to offer myself to you. He looked her up and down, then fell silent. Then a man stood, having on him but a single garment, tying its ends upon his neck, and said: If you have no need of her, marry her to me. He said to him: Do you have anything? He said: No. He said: She must have something, so go and seek. So he went and sought, but found nothing. He returned and said: I found nothing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and seek, even an iron ring. So he went, then returned and said: I did not find even an iron ring. Then he sat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What do you have of the Qur'an? He said: Such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah. He said: I have married her to you for what you have of the Qur'an."
"5759","5751 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah with a woven cloak and said: I made this for you with my hands. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted it from her, while in need of it, and wrapped himself in it. Then he came out, and a man of his Companions said: Clothe me in it? He said: Yes. So he gave it to him. Sahl said: So I said to the man: You saw the need of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for it, then you asked him for it? He said: I saw what you saw, but I wanted to keep it hidden until I am shrouded in it. So he was shrouded in it."
"5760","5752 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, al-Layth narrated, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that some people came to him disputing about the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): of what wood is it? He said: I know of what wood it is, who made it, and the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a woman of the Ansar to command a carpenter slave boy of hers, so he made for him wooden steps upon which he addresses the people. So he made it for him of tamarisk of al-Ghaba. When he finished it, the woman informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of it. So he sent for it and it was carried, and he addressed the people upon it. Then prayer was established, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uttered the takbir while upon the minbar, then bowed upon it, then descended for prostration and prostrated, then bowed upon the minbar, and did the like thereof until he finished his prayer."
"5761","5753 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, Harun ibn Musa al-Farawi narrated, my father narrated, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"5762","5754 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Burjani, Yahya ibn Hakim al-Muqawwim narrated, al-Husayn ibn Hafs al-Asbahani narrated, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise has a gate called al-Rayyan; the fasting are called to it; whoever is of the fasting enters it and never thirsts again."
"5763","5755 - Narrated Tahir ibn Isa ibn Qayras al-Misri, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Hisham ibn Sa'd informed me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, on the day the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was struck, would burn a mat and treat his wound with it, sticking it upon him."
"5764","Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i from Abu Hazim. 5756 - Narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, both said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Musa ibn Ya'qub informed, Abu Hazim ibn Dinar narrated to me, Sahl ibn Sa'd informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two are not rejected, or he said: are not turned back: supplication at the call to prayer, and at battle when some clash with others."
"5765","Musa ibn Ya'qub said: And Razzaq ibn Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: And under the rain. Abu al-Qasim said: Razzaq has no supported hadith except this hadith, and another disconnected hadith."
"5766","5757 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated, both said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated, Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will console one another after me with condolence for me. The people would say: What is this? When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken, people met one another consoling one another for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5767","5758 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated, both said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated, Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the staff that was in the maqsura was made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he grew old; he would lean upon it when he stood. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken, it was stolen; it was sought and found in the mosque of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and termites had afflicted it."
"5768","5759 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Ja'far ibn Musafir narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Musa ibn Ya'qub, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, entered upon Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while Hasan and Husayn were weeping. He said: What makes them weep? She said: Hunger. He said: Then send to your father. So she sent, and the messenger came to him while before him was leftover dates. He said: Your daughter says, O Messenger of Allah: If you have anything, convey it to us, for Hasan and Husayn are weeping. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the messenger and he carried it to them both. He brought it to Fatima. Ali entered upon her while it was before her. Ali said: Did he find nothing but this? Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, said: No. Ali said: There is nothing in this to quiet them. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, went out and found a dinar in the market. He brought it to Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, informed her, and said: This is the dinar. Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, said: Go with it to so-and-so the Jew, and take flour from him for us. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, went out and came to the Jew and bought flour with it. When he finished, the Jew said: Are you the son-in-law of this man who claims he is the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: Then take your dinar, and the flour is yours. So Ali went out until he brought it to Fatima and informed her, and said: This is the dinar. Fatima said: Go with it to so-and-so the butcher, and take for us meat for a dirham; we shall send to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he eats with us. So he went and pawned the dinar for a dirham. He brought it; she kneaded, set up, and baked. She sent to her father, and he came to her; lo, a bowl containing bread, lo, the meat boiling, and lo, flour. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I mention to you; if you deem it lawful for us, we eat and you eat; its story is such-and-such. He said: Eat in the name of Allah. So they ate. While they were in their place, lo, a boy seeking the dinar by Allah and by Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded, and he was called for him, and he asked him. He said: My family sent me with a dinar to buy with it, and it fell from me in the market. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go to the butcher and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Send me the dinar, and your dirham is upon me. So he sent it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed it to him."
"5769","5760 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Duhaym narrated, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, from Musa ibn Ya'qub, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every people have a forerunner, and I am your forerunner at the Hawd. Whoever comes to me at the Hawd and drinks, shall never thirst; and whoever never thirsts enters Paradise."
"5770","Hammad ibn Abi Humayd, and he is Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd al-Madani, from Abu Hazim. 5761 - Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated, Hammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I attend Fajr, then sit remembering Allah until the sun rises, is dearer to me than to mount upon fine horses in the path of Allah until the sun rises."
"5771","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from Abu Hazim. 5762 - Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, Musaddad narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will see the chamber of the chambers of Paradise as they see the setting brilliant star, east and west."
"5772","5763 - Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, Musaddad narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), women were commanded in prayer not to raise their heads until the men took their seats upon the ground, on account of the looseness of garments."
"5773","5764 - Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, Musaddad narrated, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise has a gate called al-Rayyan. It will be said on the Day of Resurrection: Where are the fasting? When they enter, it is closed, and none besides them enters through it."
"5774","5765 - Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated, Khalid informed, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Clapping is for women, and glorification is for men."
"5775","5766 - Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, Musaddad narrated; and narrated Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated, both said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that men of the Muslims used to attend prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), tying their cloaks, with upon none of them but a single garment."
"5776","5767 - Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated, from Abbad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have committed adultery with so-and-so, naming her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to the woman and asked her, but she denied. So he stoned him and left her."
"5777","Malik ibn Anas from Abu Hazim. 5768 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People remain in good so long as they hasten the fast-breaking."
"5778","5769 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drink and drank from it, while to his right was a boy, and to his left the elders. He said to the boy: Do you permit me to give these? The boy said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I shall not prefer anyone over my share from you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed it in his hand."
"5779","5770 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it be, then in the horse, the woman, and the dwelling, meaning ill omen."
"5780","5771 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik; and narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, Malik informed; and narrated Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, Malik narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to Banu Amr ibn Awf to reconcile between them, and prayer time came. The mu'adhdhin came to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Will you pray for the people so I establish prayer? He said: Yes. So Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, prayed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while the people were in prayer, and slipped through until he stood in the row. The people clapped, while Abu Bakr would not turn in his prayer. When the people clapped much, Abu Bakr turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to stay firm in your place. So Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, raised his hands and praised Allah Almighty for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had commanded him of that. Then he stepped back until he stood straight in the row, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed. Then he finished and said: O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from staying firm when I commanded you? He said: It would not befit Ibn Abi Quhafa to pray before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did I see you clap so much? Whoever is beset by something in his prayer, let him glorify Allah; for when he glorifies, he is attended to; and clapping is only for women."
"5781","5772 - Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: People were commanded that a man place his right hand upon his left forearm."
"5782","5773 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmala ibn Yahya, my grandfather Harmala ibn Yahya narrated, Ibn Wahb and Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafi'i narrated, both said: Malik ibn Anas narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Bilal calls at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"5783","5774 - Narrated Musa ibn Jumhur al-Tinnisi, Mu'ammal ibn Ihab narrated, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated, Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two hours, the supplication of a supplicant is not turned back therein: when night prayer is established, and in the ranks in the path of Allah."
"5784","5775 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated, Muhammad ibn Khalid narrated, Malik ibn Anas narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by boys playing with dust, and some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them. He said: Leave them, for dust is the springtime of boys."
"5785","5776 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Asbahani, Yasin ibn Abd al-Ahad al-Misri narrated, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated, Malik ibn Anas narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will see the people of the chambers above them as you see the brilliant vanishing star on the horizon, east and west, on account of the disparity between them."
"5786","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhi'b from Abu Hazim. 5777 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from Salama ibn Dinar, Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that Uwaymir al-Ajlani came to Asim ibn Adi and said: What do you think of a man who finds another man with his wife; if he kills him, will you kill him? Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me. So Asim asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked such questions and censured them. Asim informed Uwaymir. Uwaymir said: By Allah, I shall surely come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he came, while the Qur'an had come down. He asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Qur'an has indeed come down concerning you two. So step forward and invoke li'an. Then he said: I have lied against her if I keep her. So he separated from her, though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not command him to separate from her. So it became a sunna concerning the two invoking li'an. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch her; if she bears him red, short, as if a wahara, then I consider him lying against her; and if she bears him dark, large-eyed, with buttocks, then I consider him truthful against her. So she came of the disliked description."
"5787","Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif from Abu Hazim. 5778 - Narrated Yahya ibn Salih, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated, Abu Hazim narrated, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"5788","5779 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan informed, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My minbar is upon a channel of the channels of Paradise."
"5789","5780 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a cup and drank, while to his right was a boy of the youngest of the people, and the elders to his left. He said: O boy, do you permit me to give it to the elders? He said: I would not prefer anyone over my privilege in you, O Messenger of Allah. So he gave it to him."
"5790","5781 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that a woman offered herself to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man of the people said: Marry her to me. He said: What do you have? He said: I have nothing. He said: Go and seek, even an iron ring. So he went, then returned and said: By Allah, I found nothing, nor an iron ring; but this is my waist-wrapper, half of it is hers. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What will you do with your waist-wrapper? If you wear it, there will be nothing of it upon her; and if she wears it, there will be nothing of it upon you. So the man sat until his sitting grew long. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, and called him, or he was brought. He said to him: What do you have of the Qur'an? He said: With me is such-and-such surah and such-and-such. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have married her to you for what you have of the Qur'an."
"5791","5782 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan informed, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand, or seven hundred thousand, of my umma shall surely enter Paradise, holding one another, until the first of them and the last of them enter Paradise, their faces like the moon on the night of full moon."
"5792","5783 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan informed, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd; whoever passes by me drinks, and whoever drinks never thirsts again. Some people whom I know and who know me shall surely come to me, then a barrier is placed between me and them."
"5793","5784 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that a man was of the greatest of the Muslims in availing the Muslims in a campaign he fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked and said: Whoever wishes to look at a man of the people of Hellfire, let him look at this one. A man of the people followed him, while he was in that state, of the fiercest of people against the polytheists, until he was wounded. He hastened death, so he took the point of his sword and placed it between his breasts until it came out from between his shoulders. The man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastening and said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what is that? He said: You said: Whoever wishes to look at a man of the people of Hellfire, let him look at this one, while he was of the greatest of us in availing the Muslims. So I knew he would not die upon that. When he was wounded he hastened death and killed himself. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said thereupon: A servant may do the deeds of the people of Paradise while he is of the people of Hellfire, and may do the deeds of the people of Hellfire while he is of the people of Paradise; deeds are only by their endings."
"5794","5785 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a woven cloak. Sahl said to the people: Do you know what a burd is? The people said: It is a woven wrap, with its border in it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to clothe you in this. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it, in need of it, and wore it. A man of his Companions saw it upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, how fine this is; clothe me in it. He said: Yes. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, his Companions blamed him and said: You did not do well when you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take it in need of it, then asked him for it, though you knew he is never asked anything but he withholds. He said: By Allah, nothing prompted me to that except I hoped for its blessing when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore it, that I might be shrouded in it."
"5795","5786 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan informed, Abu Hazim narrated, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that between the mosque on the qibla side and the qibla was the passage of a sheep."
"5796","5787 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan informed, Abu Hazim narrated, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: We used to pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the midday rest would follow."
"5797","5788 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan informed, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: There was a woman among us who would plant beets in a farm of hers. When Friday came, she would pull the beet roots and place them in a pot, then place over them a handful of barley and cook it; so the beet roots were its fat. Sahl said: We would return to her from Friday prayer and greet her, and she would bring that food near to us. We used to long for Friday on account of that food of hers."
"5798","5789 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan informed, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The helmet was crushed upon the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud, his incisor was broken, and his face wounded. Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would wash the blood from him, and Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, would bring her water. When water touched the wound, its blood flowed and would not stop, until she took a piece of mat and burned it until it became ash, then placed it upon the wound, and the blood stopped."
"5799","5790 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan informed, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a woman of the Muhajirin who had a carpenter slave. He said to her: Command your slave to make for me wood like a minbar. So she commanded her slave; he went to al-Ghaba, cut of tamarisk, and made a minbar for him. When he finished it, she sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he had finished it. He said: So it was sent to me; they brought it to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried it and placed it where you see."
"5800","5791 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Abu Ghassan informed, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: When this verse came down: And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread, while from the dawn had not yet come down, men, when they intended to fast, would tie in their legs a black thread and a white thread, and keep eating and drinking until one of them became distinct to him. Then Allah revealed afterwards: From the dawn. So they knew it only means night and day."
"5801","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Abu Ghassan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: An Arab woman was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi to send for her. He sent for her and she came, and she stayed with Banu Sa'ida. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out until he came to her, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to her, she said: I seek refuge with Allah from you. He said: You have indeed been granted refuge from me. They said to her: Do you know who this is? This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he has come to propose to you. She said: If I am more wretched than that. Sahl said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came that day until he sat in the shed of Banu Sa'ida, he and his Companions, then he said: Give us drink, O Abu Sa'd. He said: So I brought out this cup for them and gave them drink in it. Abu Hazim said: So Sahl brought out that cup for us and we drank in it, then Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, afterwards asked him for it as a gift, and he gave it to him."
"5802","Narrated Yahya ibn Salih from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Abu Ghassan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: Al-Mundhir ibn Abi Usayd was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was born, and he placed him on his thigh while Abu Usayd was sitting. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became distracted by something in front of him, so Abu Usayd ordered that his son be taken, and he was carried away from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they turned him away, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and said: Where is the boy? Abu Usayd said: We have taken him away, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What is his name? He said: So-and-so. He said: No, rather his name is al-Mundhir. So he named him al-Mundhir that day."
"5803","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Abu Ghassan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: When Abu Sahl Usayd al-Sa'idi married, he invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, and he prepared food for them, and none served it to them except his wife Umm Usayd. And she soaked some dates overnight in a stone vessel, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the food, she brought it to him and gave him drink."
"5804","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Abu Ghassan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there are eight gates; one of them is called al-Rayyan; none shall enter it except those who fast."
"5805","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Abu Ghassan from Abu Hazim, who said: I asked Sahl ibn Sa'd: Did you see fine sifted wheat in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: No. Abu Hazim said: So I said: How did you sift barley? He said: No, but we used to blow it."
"5806","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Mukram and Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi, both saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated from Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An evening stroll in the path of Allah or a morning stroll is better than the world and what is in it."
"5807","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi from Ali ibn al-Ja'd from Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif from Abu Hazim from Sahl, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do, in what people see, the deeds of the people of Paradise, yet he is of the people of Hell; and he may do, in what people see, the deeds of the people of Hell, yet he is of the people of Paradise; and deeds are only by their endings."
"5808","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, both saying: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Hubuli narrated from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Shirazi from Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do, in what people see, the deeds of the people of Paradise yet he is of the people of Hell; and he may do, in what people see, the deeds of the people of Hell yet he is of the people of Paradise; and deeds are only by their endings."
"5809","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, both saying: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Halabi narrated from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Shirazi from Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."
"5810","Narrated Abdullah ibn Nahiya from Ahmad ibn Mani' from Husayn ibn Muhammad from Abu Ghassan from Abu Hazim that he saw Sahl ibn Sa'd urinate standing, then wipe over his leather socks. So I said: What is this, O Abu al-Abbas? He said: I saw one better than me wipe over them."
"5811","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, both saying: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated; and narrated Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari from Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar, both saying: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated from Musa ibn Ubayda al-Rabadhi from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, and from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, both saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, is behind seventy thousand veils of light and darkness, and no soul hears anything of the sound of those veils but that it perishes."
"5812","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Hammad ibn al-Hasan al-Warraq from Sa'id ibn Sallam al-Attar from Umar ibn Muhammad from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If bad omen is in anything, then it is in the woman, the horse, and the house."
"5813","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Hammad ibn al-Hasan al-Warraq from Sa'id ibn Sallam al-Attar from Umar ibn Muhammad from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hud and its sisters have made me grey: al-Waqi'a, al-Haqqa, and When the sun is folded up."
"5814","Narrated Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Isma'il al-Razi from Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Bakr al-Razi from his father from Umar ibn Muhammad from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until it was said: He does not break fast, and he would break fast until it was said: He does not fast; and most of his fasting was in Sha'ban."
"5815","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Khalid ibn Makhlad from Sulayman ibn Bilal from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise in what appears to people, yet he is of the people of Hell; and a man may do the deeds of the people of Hell in what appears to people, yet he is of the people of Paradise."
"5816","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani from Sulayman ibn Bilal from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: When bad omen was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If it is in anything, then it is in the woman, the dwelling, and the horse."
"5817","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani from Sulayman ibn Bilal from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard him say: The dearest of Ali's names, may Allah be pleased with him, to him was Abu Turab, and he used to rejoice at being called by it; and none named him Abu Turab except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One day he was angry with Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, so he went out and lay down by the wall. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came seeking him but did not find him in the house, so he said to Fatima: Where is your cousin? She said: He went out just now in anger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a man with him to seek him. He said: He is lying by the wall; his cloak has slipped from his back and it is filled with dust. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began wiping the dust from his back, saying: Sit, O Abu Turab."
"5818","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani from Sulayman ibn Bilal from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pulpit is upon a channel of the channels of Paradise."
"5819","Narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Mudari from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Aslam narrated, Abu Hazim narrated to me, Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall be in the end of time sinking, pelting, and transformation. It was said: And when is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When musical instruments and singing women appear, and wine is deemed lawful."
"5820","Narrated Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Qazzaz from Ishaq ibn Idris from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to bracelet his child with two bracelets of fire, let him bracelet him with a bracelet of gold; but play with silver and white silver as you wish."
"5821","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi from Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: With Allah are the treasuries of good and evil; their keys are men. So blessed is he whom He makes a key to good and a lock to evil, and woe to he whom He makes a key to evil and a lock to good."
"5822","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Abu Kamil al-Jahdari from Abdullah ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uhud is a pillar of the pillars of Paradise."
"5823","Narrated Ahmad ibn Anbar al-Basri from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Abdullah ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand upon his pulpit and pray for the people while upon the pulpit; he said takbir while upon it, then bowed, then stepped back backwards and prostrated at the foot of the pulpit, then returned and did the like until he finished his prayer. Then he turned to the people and said: O people, I did this only so that you follow me and learn my prayer."
"5824","Narrated Ahmad ibn Anbar from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Abdullah ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: A cup was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he drank, while the elders were on his left and a boy, the youngest of the people, on his right. When he drank he said: O boy, do you permit me to give to the elders? He said: I would not prefer anyone with my share of your surplus, O Messenger of Allah. So he gave it to him."
"5825","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman from Abdullah ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: There was a dispute among the Ansar, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them to make peace between them. Then he returned after the prayer had been established, with Abu Bakr praying with the people, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"5826","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm from Sahl ibn Uthman from Abdullah ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim, who said: I saw Sahl ibn Sa'd, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), urinate while standing, the urination of a very old man which almost precedes him, then perform ablution and wipe over the leather socks. So I said to him: Will you not remove them? He said: No; I have seen one better than me wipe over them."
"5827","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm from Sahl ibn Uthman from Abdullah ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Khaybar: I shall give the banner tomorrow to a man through whose hands Allah will grant victory. The people spent the night wondering which of them would be given it. When morning came they went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Where is Ali? They said: He is here, O Messenger of Allah, with sore eyes complaining of his eyes. He sent for him, spat in his eyes, and supplicated with whatever Allah willed, and he was healed until there was no pain in him. Then he gave him the banner and said: Go forward. He said to him: O Messenger of Allah, shall I fight them until they become like us? He said: Proceed gently until you alight in their courtyard, then invite them to Islam and inform them of what is due upon them of the right of Allah therein. For that Allah guide through you a single man is better for you than red camels."
"5828","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm from Sahl ibn Uthman from Abdullah ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan. It shall be said on the Day of Resurrection: Where are those who fast? Is there for you a way to al-Rayyan? Whoever enters through it shall never thirst again. They shall enter through it, and when the last of them has entered it shall be closed, and none besides them shall enter through it."
"5829","Narrated Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Bahrani from Abu Amir al-Aqadi from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabra, who said: Abu Hazim narrated to me from Sahl ibn Sa'd that an old, swollen, yellowed shaykh whose veins had appeared was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had committed adultery with a woman, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck him with a palm-branch cluster containing a hundred twigs in a single stroke."
"5830","Narrated Ishaq ibn Dawud from Muhammad ibn Ma'mar from Abu Amir from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabra from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I witnessed Ma'iz when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his stoning. He ran, and the people followed him stoning him, until Umar met him in the desert graveyard and struck him with a camel's jawbone and killed him."
"5831","Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi from Abu Hazim, who said: I saw Sahl ibn Sa'd urinate standing; and he had grown old until he could hardly control it. He said: Then he called for water, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks. So I said: Will you not remove your leather socks? He said: I saw one better than me do that."
"5832","Narrated Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi from Abdullah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: When it was the day of Uhud and the polytheists turned away from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, the women went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions to aid them. Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was among those who went out. When she met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) she embraced him and began washing his wounds with water, and the blood increased. When she saw that, she took a piece of mat, burnt it with fire, and pressed it until it stuck to the wound and the blood stopped."
"5833","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is beset by something in his prayer, let him glorify Allah, saying: Subhan Allah; for glorification is for men and clapping is for women."
"5834","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani from Ibn Wahb from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise in what appears to people, yet he is of the people of Hell; and a man may do the deeds of the people of Hell in what appears to people, yet he is of the people of Paradise."
"5835","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Sa'id ibn Sulayman from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan; none shall enter through it except those who fast, and when they have entered through it, it shall be closed."
"5836","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba from Zayd ibn al-Hubab from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi, who said: I heard Abu Hazim say: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, mentioning Paradise: In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has not occurred to a human heart."
"5837","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Shu'ayb ibn Salama al-Ansari from Abu Mus'ab Isma'il ibn Qays from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for emigration, and he said to him: O uncle, remain in your place where you are, for Allah shall seal emigration with you as He sealed prophethood with me."
"5838","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Sa'id ibn Sulayman from Abu Mus'ab Isma'il ibn Qays from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from one of his expeditions on a hot day, and water was placed for him to cool himself with. Abbas, may Allah have mercy on him, came, turned his back to him, and shaded him with a cloak he had on. He said: Who is this? He said: Your uncle Abbas, O Messenger of Allah. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he raised his hands until they appeared to us from the cloak, and said: May Allah shield you, O uncle, and your offspring from the Fire."
"5839","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we met the polytheists we fought them until we and they separated at evening, both parties exhausted and weary, except a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who did not slacken nor tire; he left none scattered nor isolated of the people but that he killed them. The people marveled at his endurance, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to look at a man of the people of Hell, let him look at this. A man of the people said: By Allah, I shall be his companion until I see what becomes of him. He was wounded and panicked at death, so he took his sword, placed it upon his liver, then leaned upon it until he drove it through his back. The man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant may do acts of obedience to Allah, mighty and majestic, in what appears to people, yet he is written with Allah among the people of Hell; and a servant may do acts of disobedience to Allah in what appears to people, yet he is written with Allah among the people of Paradise."
"5840","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People shall be gathered on the Day of Resurrection upon a white land like a loaf of sifted flour."
"5841","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin from Sa'id ibn Maryam from Muhammad ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: Bad omen was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If it is in anything, then it is in the woman, the dwelling, and the horse."
"5842","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day with the people behind him, and he kept praying then stepping back backwards."
"5843","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Khalid ibn Makhlad from Muhammad ibn Ja'far from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Pond; whoever comes to me shall drink, and whoever drinks shall never thirst. Yet there shall come to me peoples whom I know by recognition, then they shall be barred from me."
"5844","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Attaf ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A morning stroll in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and an evening stroll in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and the space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"5845","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Makhlad ibn Malik al-Harrani from Attaf ibn Khalid from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and he mentioned the like."
"5846","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi from Ibrahim ibn Khalid from Abdullah ibn Mus'ab from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married a man to a woman for an iron ring whose stone was of silver."
"5847","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr from Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi from Ibrahim ibn Khalid from Abdullah ibn Mus'ab from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: What do you think of the worthlessness of this to its owners? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a dead sheep. He said: By Allah, the world is more worthless to Allah than this is to its owners."
"5848","Narrated Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari from al-Humaydi; and narrated Abdullah ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, both saying: Zakariyya ibn Manzur al-Qurazi narrated, Abu Hazim narrated to me from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a slave for Allah, Allah shall free for each limb of it a limb of him from the Fire."
"5849","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi from Hisham ibn Ammar; and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Sa'id ibn Sulayman, both saying: Zakariyya ibn Manzur narrated from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Dhu al-Hulayfa and there was a dead sheep lifting its leg. He said: Do you see this sheep as insignificant to its owners? They said: Yes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this sheep is to its owners; and if the world weighed with Allah the wing of a gnat, He would not give a disbeliever a drink of water from it."
"5850","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami from Ma'mar ibn Bakkar al-Sa'di from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in good and evil."
"5851","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki from Sa'id ibn Mansur from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman, brother of Fulayh, from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A morning stroll in the path of Allah or an evening stroll is better than the world and what is in it."
"5852","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman, brother of Fulayh, from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: A dispute occurred among Banu Amr ibn Awf until they pelted one another with stones. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he went out to make peace between them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delayed until Bilal called the adhan for prayer, then he came to Abu Bakr and said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been delayed; will you establish the prayer? Abu Bakr said: Yes. He established the prayer, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stepped forward, said takbir, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appeared. The people clapped for Abu Bakr, and he would not turn in his prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threaded through the people until Abu Bakr heard his movement behind him, so he went to step back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As you are, O Abu Bakr; pray with us. Abu Bakr raised his hand to the sky to step back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed with the people. When he finished he said: O Abu Bakr, what prevented you, when I commanded you to pray with the people, from praying with them? He said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, it was not fitting for the son of Abu Quhafa to pray before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Did you stretch your hands to the sky? He said: I praised Allah when you commanded me to pray with you. Then he turned to the people and said: O people, what is with you that when something befalls you in your prayer you take to clapping? Clapping is only for women; whoever is beset by something in his prayer, let him glorify Allah, and let the one next to him turn to him."
"5853","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal; and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, both saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated from Hushaym from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a matter confuses you, you take to clapping; if a matter confuses you in your prayer, then glorification is for men and clapping is for women."
"5854","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Muhammad ibn Sabur al-Raqqi from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a pasture of musk like the pasture of your animals in the world."
"5855","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Sa'id ibn Sulayman from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim, who said: I said to Sahl ibn Sa'd: Were there sieves in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I never saw a sieve in that time, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate sifted barley until he left the world. I said: What did you do? He said: We used to grind it, then blow it, and what flew away flew, and what remained remained."
"5856","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Sa'id ibn Sulayman; and narrated Abdan from Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn; and narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abdan ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi, all saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two hours in which supplication is not rejected: at prayer and at fighting."
"5857","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Sa'id ibn Sulayman from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate to fullness twice in a day until he left the world."
"5858","Narrated Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We used to rejoice at Friday. I said to him: And what was that? He said: There was a woman of the neighborhood who would take chard and pour it over barley between vinegar; when it was Friday she would pull it by its roots, sprinkle over it some barley, then place it in her pot, then put it in her oven and serve it to us. We used to call it drowned chard, and we would lick it; and we used to rejoice at Friday because of her pot. And the midday nap for lunch on Friday was after Friday, after the prayer, in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5859","Narrated Sadaqa ibn Muhammad ibn Kharuf al-Misri from Abd al-Mun'im ibn Bashir al-Ansari from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not enter the houses of the people of dhimma except with permission."
"5860","Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani from Sa'id ibn Sulayman from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast when Safiyya came to him. I said: What was in his feast? He said: It was nothing but dates and sawiq."
"5861","Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani from Sa'id ibn Sulayman from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: Bad omen was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If it is in anything, then it is in the dwelling, the horse, and the woman."
"5862","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Sulayman ibn Salama al-Khaba'iri from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman al-Madani from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walk behind the funeral bier."
"5863","Narrated Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri from Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Wasiti al-Naqid from Yazid ibn Harun from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his Companions were with him; she circled them but found no place. A man noticed her, stood up, and she sat. She relieved her need then stood. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: Do you know her? He said: No. He said: Did you show her mercy? May Allah have mercy on you — three times."
"5864","Narrated Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Qazzaz from Ishaq ibn Idris from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married a woman of the desert people, then saw whiteness upon her, so he separated from her before consummating with her."
"5865","Narrated Abdullah ibn Najiya from Ahmad ibn Mani' from Ya'qub ibn al-Walid al-Madani from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning stroll in the path of Allah or an evening stroll is better than the world and what is in it."
"5866","Narrated Abdullah ibn Najiya from Ahmad ibn Mani' from Ya'qub ibn al-Walid from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you is beset by something in his prayer, let him glorify Allah; for glorification is for men and clapping is for women."
"5867","Narrated Abdullah ibn Najiya from Ahmad ibn Mani' from Ya'qub ibn al-Walid from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"5868","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Nafi' Darakht from Ya'qub ibn al-Walid from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat melon with fresh dates."
"5869","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama from Ubaydullah ibn Musa from Abd al-Salam ibn Mus'ab from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray toward Bayt al-Maqdis; when he was turned, a man set out to the people of Quba and found them praying the dawn prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been commanded to pray toward the Ka'ba. So their imam turned around until he faced with them the qibla."
"5870","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi from Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi from Zuhra ibn Amr ibn Ma'bad al-Taymi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it, and a morning stroll in the path of Allah or an evening stroll is better than the world and what is in it."
"5871","And with his chain: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when his front tooth was broken, his face wounded, the helmet crushed upon his head. And I know who washed the blood from his face, who carried water to him, and what was placed upon his wound until the blood stopped. Fatima, daughter of Muhammad the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would wash the blood from his face, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, would carry water to her in a shield. When she had washed the blood from her father's face she burnt a mat, until when it had become ash she took some of that ash and placed it upon his face until the blood stopped. Then he said that day: Allah's anger intensified upon a people who wounded the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he remained a while, then said: O Allah, forgive my people, for they do not know."
"5872","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Ma'ni from Sulaym ibn Qutayba from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that Abu Usayd married and invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his wedding. His wife would serve us, giving us to drink an infusion she had soaked overnight, and she gave him drink."
"5873","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, both saying: al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated from Hassan ibn Ibrahim from Sa'id ibn Khalid al-Madani from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a hump, and the hump of the Qur'an is Surat al-Baqara. Whoever recites it in his house at night, no devil shall enter it for three nights; and whoever recites it in his house by day, no devil shall enter it for three days."
"5874","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama from Ubaydullah ibn Musa from Abdullah ibn Amir from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The midday nap in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was after Friday."
"5875","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib from Wahb ibn Uthman from Abu Hazim, who said: We were with Sahl ibn Sa'd at a funeral and he narrated to them, then said: Shall I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while you are distracted? By Allah, I shall surely leave you. He said: Where to? He said: To fight. I said: And is that in you? He said: I shall increase the multitude of the Muslims."
"5876","Narrated Muhammad ibn Zurayq ibn Jami' al-Misri and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, both saying: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated from Abu Sulaym Bakr ibn Sulaym al-Sawwaf from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began strange and shall return strange; so blessed are the strangers. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and who are the strangers? He said: Those who set right when people are corrupt."
"5877","Narrated Muhammad ibn Zurayq from Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh from Bakr ibn Sulaym from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day while we were in a gathering in which were Amr ibn al-As and his son. He said: How will you be when you are left behind in a time of the dregs of people whose covenants and vows have become mixed and entangled, and they become like this? And he interlaced his fingers. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Take what you recognize, leave what you disapprove, let each of you attend to his private self and leave the affair of the multitude."
"5878","Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali from Abu Ma'shar from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib brought water in a shield — meaning a buckler — on the day of Uhud, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his face, and said: This is water that has become stale — meaning changed. He said: And Fatima took a piece of mat, burnt it, and placed it upon his wound."
"5879","And with his chain he said: A dispute occurred between Ali and Fatima, may Allah be pleased with them both. Ali went out in anger and threw himself upon the dust. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked her, and she said: There was a dispute between me and him and he went out in anger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and found him sleeping upon the dust. He woke him and began wiping the dust from his back, saying: You are but Abu Turab. Sahl ibn Sa'd said: We used to praise him with it, yet people now blame him with it."
"5880","Narrated Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk from Ali ibn al-Madini from Abu Damra Anas ibn Iyad from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I used to take suhur with my family, then my haste would be to catch the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5881","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd; and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Hakim al-Warraq, both saying: Anas ibn Iyad narrated from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of belittled sins; for the likeness of belittled sins is like a people who alighted in the belly of a valley: this one came with a stick and that one came with a stick, until they carried what they ripened their bread with. And belittled sins, whenever their doer is seized by them, destroy him."
"5882","Narrated Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamza al-Zubayri from his father from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two."
"5883","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Amr ibn Awn from Hushaym from Abu Yahya from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Companions and whoever saw one who saw me. He said: I said: And what is his saying: And whoever saw? He said: Whoever saw one who saw them."
"5884","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qa'nabi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were digging the Trench and carrying dust upon our shoulders. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no life but the life of the Hereafter; so forgive the Emigrants and the Helpers."
"5885","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin from Ibrahim ibn Hammad ibn Abi Hazim al-Madani from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, uncircumcised."
"5886","Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam and Yahya ibn Bukayr — Yahya saying: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated, and Sa'id saying: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated — from his father that he heard Sahl say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of Khaybar: I shall give the banner to a man through whose hands Allah will grant victory. The people spent the night wondering who would be given it. When morning came the people went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each hoping to be given it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is Ali ibn Abi Talib? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he complains of his eyes. He sent for him, spat in his eyes, and supplicated for him, and he was healed on the spot as if there had been nothing in him. He gave him the banner, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I fight them until they become like us? He said: Proceed gently until you alight in their courtyard, then invite them to Islam and inform them of what is due upon them therein of right. By Allah, that Allah guide through your guidance a man is better for you than red camels."
"5887","Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise shall see the chamber in Paradise as you see the stars in the sky."
"5888","Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub from Yahya ibn Bukayr from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd that a man came to him and said: This so-and-so, an amir of the amirs of Medina, invites you tomorrow to revile Ali at the pulpit. He said: So what shall I say? He said: Say: Abu Turab. Sahl laughed, then said: By Allah, none named him that except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Allah, there was no name dearer to him than it. Abd al-Aziz said: So my father said: O Abu al-Abbas, how was that? He said: Ali entered upon Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then went out and lay down in the mosque. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Fatima and said: Where is your cousin? She said: He is there in the mosque. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and found his cloak had fallen from his back and dust had reached his back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began wiping the dust from his back, saying: Sit, Abu Turab; sit, Abu Turab. By Allah, there was no name dearer to him than it; none named him that except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5889","Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf from Sa'id ibn Maryam; and narrated Abu Husayn from al-Himmani, both saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People shall remain upon good so long as they hasten the breaking of fast and do not delay it as the people of the East delay it."
"5890","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim, who said: My father narrated to me that he heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi ask about the pulpit: Of what wood is it? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to so-and-so, a woman he named, and said: Order your carpenter slave to make for me steps upon which I address the people. So he made for him these three steps of tamarisk of the thicket. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them — meaning the steps — and they were placed in this spot. Sahl said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the first day he sat upon them: he said takbir, and the people said takbir behind him, then he bowed while upon the pulpit, then raised his head, came down backwards, and prostrated at the foot of the pulpit, then returned until he finished the end of his prayer, doing in it as he did in the first rak'a. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he turned to the people and said: O people, I did this only so that you follow me and learn my prayer."
"5891","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Sufyan from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim from his father that he heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever is beset by something in his prayer, let him say: Subhan Allah; and clapping is for women."
"5892","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he looked at him, then said: What is your opinion of this? I said: This is a man of the nobles of people; he is fit, if he proposes, to be married, if he intercedes, to be granted intercession, and if he speaks, for his word to be heard. Then a man passed, and he said: What is your opinion of this? I said: This is a man of the poor Muslims; he is fit, if he speaks, for his word not to be heard, if he proposes, not to be married, and if he intercedes, not to be granted intercession. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one is better than the earth full of the like of that one."
"5893","And from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in station — and there is none lowly therein — is he who wishes, speaking with a fluent, eloquent tongue and a composed mind: Give me, give me such-and-such, until when he finds nothing he is prompted and told: Say: Such-and-such, say: Such-and-such. Then it is said to him: It is yours, and the like of it with it."
"5894","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qa'nabi from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two — and he pointed with his two fingers."
"5895","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from al-Qa'nabi from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"5896","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd that a woman brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a woven cloak with its border in it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I wove this with my hand and have come with it to clothe you with it. So-and-so — a man he named — touched it and said: O Messenger of Allah, how beautiful this cloak is; clothe me with it? He said: Yes. When he entered he folded it and sent it to him. The people said: By Allah, you did not do well; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was clothed with it while in need of it, then you asked him for it though you knew he does not turn away a asker? He said: By Allah, I did not ask him for it to wear it, but I asked him for it that it be my shroud the day I die. Sahl said: And it was his shroud the day he died."
"5897","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We used to say: The pulpit is upon a channel of the channels of Paradise. Sahl said: Do you know what the channel is? It is the gate."
"5898","And with his chain: I asked Sahl: Did you see sifted flour? He said: I never saw sifted flour until Allah took the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Did you have sieves in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I never saw a sieve until Allah took His Messenger. I said: How do you eat unsifted barley? He said: Yes, we blow it, then what flies of it flies."
"5899","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from al-Himmani, both saying: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a cup with water in it and drank from it, with on his right a boy, the youngest of the people, and the elders on his left. When he finished he said: O boy, do you permit me to give to the elders? The boy said: I would not prefer anyone with your surplus. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thrust it into the hand of the boy."
"5900","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise in what you see, yet he is of the people of Hell; and a man may do the deeds of the people of Hell in what you see, yet he is of the people of Paradise."
"5901","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki from Ya'qub ibn Humayd; and narrated Abu Husayn from Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning stroll in the path of Allah or an evening stroll is better than the world and what is in it."
"5902","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr from Ya'qub from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi married, and his wife made an infusion overnight; when morning came she strained it, and she gave it to drink to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5903","And from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Pond; whoever comes to me shall drink, and whoever drinks shall never thirst again. See that there do not come to me peoples whom I know and who know me, then they are barred from me."
"5904","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani; and narrated al-Fadl ibn Abi Rawh al-Basri from Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban, both saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated, who said: I heard my father say: I saw Sahl ibn Sa'd urinate the urination of a very old man which almost precedes him, standing, then perform ablution and wipe over the leather socks. So I said: Will you not remove them? He said: I saw one better than me and than you do this."
"5905","Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani; and narrated al-Fadl ibn Abi Rawh al-Basri from Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban, both saying: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated, who said: I heard my father narrate from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: Between the prayer spot of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the wall was the space of a sheep's passage."
"5906","Narrated al-Fadl ibn Abi Rawh al-Basri from Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban from Ibn Abi Hazim, who said: I heard my father narrate from Sahl ibn Sa'd that he was asked about the wound of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud. He said: His face was wounded, his front tooth broken, the helmet crushed upon his head. Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would wash the blood, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, would pour upon her with the shield. When Fatima saw that water only increased the blood, she took a piece of mat, burnt it until it became ash, then stuck it to the wound and the blood stopped."
"5907","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal from Ya'qub ibn Humayd from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand and seven hundred thousand of my umma shall enter Paradise, holding to one another, as if their faces are the moon on the night of full moon."
"5908","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Isma'il ibn al-Hakam al-Thaqafi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of gharar."
"5909","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Isma'il ibn Abi al-Hakam al-Thaqafi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant does not believe until he believes in qadar."
"5910","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Qur'an were in a skin, the Fire would not touch it."
"5911","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We would not take the midday nap nor eat lunch except after Friday."
"5912","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal from Ya'qub ibn Humayd from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I used to take suhur with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then my haste would be only to catch the dawn prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5913","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We used to rejoice on Friday. I said: And why? He said: There was an old woman of ours who would send, take some chard roots, throw them in a pot, boil some grains of barley, and place them in it. When we had prayed Friday we would go to her, and we used to rejoice on Friday because of that; and we would not take the midday nap except after Friday."
"5914","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i; and narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and the guardian of the orphan are in Paradise like this — and he pointed with his two fingers, separating them."
"5915","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We used to say: If there is in anything — meaning bad omen — then it is in the dwelling, the woman, and the horse."
"5916","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i from Ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to offer myself to you. She stood long while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not look at her; he raised his gaze upon her and lowered it. When her standing grew long she stepped aside and sat. A man of the people stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her, marry her to me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have anything to give her as dower? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Go and look. He went, then returned and said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I found nothing. He said: Go and seek even an iron ring. He went, then returned, and said: No, by Allah, I found nothing, not even an iron ring. He said — and he had on a waist-wrapper with no cloak upon him — he said: O Messenger of Allah, my waist-wrapper. He said: Your waist-wrapper: if she wears it there shall be nothing of it upon her, and if you wear it there shall be nothing of it upon you. The man stepped aside, then stood, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him turning away, so he ordered him called. He said: What do you have of the Qur'an? He said: Such-and-such sura and such-and-such sura, of suras he enumerated. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go, for I have made her yours for what you have of the Qur'an."
"5917","And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People shall be gathered on the Day of Resurrection upon a white land like a disc of sifted flour in which there is no landmark for anyone."
"5918","And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Banu Amr ibn Awf, and prayer came. Bilal came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, prayer has come, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been detained; will you lead the people? He said: If you wish. Bilal established the prayer, and Abu Bakr stepped forward. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and the people took to clapping. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, would not turn in his prayer; when the people increased he turned, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the row. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured, and Abu Bakr raised his hand, praised Allah, then Abu Bakr stepped back backwards until he returned into the row. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed with the people. When he finished he turned to the people and said: O people, what is with you that when something befalls you in prayer you take to clapping? Clapping is only for women. Whoever is beset by something in his prayer, let him say: Subhan Allah, for none hears him but turns to him. O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from praying when I gestured to you? He said: It was not fitting for the son of Abu Quhafa to pray before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5919","Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam and Yahya ibn Bukayr, both saying: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: People did not count the number from the mission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor from his death; they counted only from his arrival in Medina."
"5920","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim from his father from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters this mosque of mine to learn good or to teach it is at the station of the mujahid in the path of Allah; and whoever enters it for other than that, of people's talk, is at the station of one who sees what pleases him while it is something other than it."
"5921","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Sufyan from Abu Hazim that he heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like this of this — and Sufyan pointed with the index and middle fingers."
"5922","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba; and narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi, both saying: Sufyan narrated from Abu Hazim, who said: They asked Sahl ibn Sa'd: Of what is the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: None of the people remains who knows it better than I; it is of the tamarisk of the thicket. So-and-so, freedman of so-and-so, made it for him. And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he ascended it: he faced the qibla and said takbir, then recited, then bowed, then came down backwards and prostrated, then ascended, then recited, then bowed, then came down backwards, then prostrated."
"5923","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Sufyan from Abu Hazim, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to make peace between Banu Amr ibn Awf over something that occurred between them, until they pelted one another with stones. Prayer came, Bilal called the adhan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delayed, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stepped forward praying with the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, threading through the rows; when he reached the row next to Abu Bakr, the people took to clapping. Abu Bakr was a man who would not turn in prayer; when he heard that he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to remain firm. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, raised his head to the sky in thanks to Allah, stepped back backwards, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he turned to us and said: O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from remaining firm when I gestured to you? He said: Allah would not see the son of Abu Quhafa before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the people and said: O people, what is with you that when something befalls you in your prayer you take to clapping? Clapping is only for women; glorification is for men. Whoever is beset by something in his prayer, let him say: Subhan Allah."
"5924","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Sufyan from Abu Hazim that he heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: I was among the people with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have offered myself to you, so give your opinion concerning me. A man stood and said: Marry her to me, O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent. Then she stood and said the like. The man said: Marry her to me, O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: Do you have anything to give her? He said: No. He said: Then go and seek something. He went, then came, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I found nothing. He said: Go and seek even an iron ring. He went, then came, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I found nothing, not even an iron ring. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have anything of the Qur'an? He said: Yes, such-and-such sura and such-and-such sura. He said: Go, for I have married her to you for what you have of the Qur'an."
"5925","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Sufyan from Abu Hazim, who said: The people differed: With what was the wound of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) treated on the day of Uhud? They asked Sahl — and he was of the last remaining of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Medina — and he said: None of the Muslims remains who knows it better than I. Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, would wash the blood from the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, would bring water in his shield. A mat was taken, burnt, and his wound stuffed with it."
"5926","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"5927","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi from Zafir ibn Sulayman from Muhammad ibn Uyayna from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd; and narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Sukkari al-Jundaysaburi from Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Hanafi from Muhammad ibn Uyayna from Abu Hazim, who said: I asked Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi: With what was the wound of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) treated on the day of Uhud? He said: None upon the face of the earth remains who knows it better than I. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, would carry water in his shield, Fatima would wash the blood, a mat was burnt, and it was stuffed with it."
"5928","Narrated Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas from Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat; and narrated Muhammad ibn Sammuyah al-Asbahani from Yunus ibn Habib, both saying: Abu Dawud narrated from Zam'a ibn Salih from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while he had a woolen cloak in the weaving."
"5929","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Khatib al-Ahwazi from Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali from Abu Amir al-Aqadi from Zam'a ibn Salih from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A suit of striped black wool was woven for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with two white wool tassels made for it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the gathering with it upon him and struck his thigh: Do you not see how beautiful this suit is? A Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, clothe me with this suit. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when asked for anything, never said No to anything asked of him. He said: Yes. He called for two fastened garments, wore them, gave the Bedouin the suit, and ordered the like woven for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while it was in the weaving."
"5930","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil from his grandfather Ubayd ibn Aqil from Zam'a ibn Salih from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the world equaled with Allah the wing of a gnat, He would not give a disbeliever anything of it."
"5931","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Harun ibn Hatim from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Mulayka from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: There was a dispute between the Ansar, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out to make peace between them. He said to Bilal: If I am detained, establish the prayer and order Abu Bakr to pray with the people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was praying with the people, and he prayed behind him."
"5932","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba; and narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, both saying: Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated, both saying: Mu'awiya ibn Hisham narrated from Abu Hafs al-Ta'ifi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts the day of Arafa, he is forgiven the sin of two consecutive years."
"5933","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying: Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated from Talq ibn Ghannam from Abd al-Salam ibn Hafs from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man came to him and confessed before him that he had committed adultery with a woman he named. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for the woman and asked her about that; she denied having committed adultery. So he flogged him the hadd and left her."
"5934","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib from Abd al-Muhaymin ibn Abbas from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was invited to the wedding feast of a man of the Ansar. We stood with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was invited, and he fed us barley bread. Then the servant who was feeding us food and giving us drink was indeed the bride herself."
"5935","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar from Abu Hazim, who said: I was with Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi when it was said to him: Was there something between Banu Amr ibn Awf and the people of Quba? He said: It was long ago; that had been. We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when one came and it was said to him: There has occurred something between the people of Quba. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out to them to make peace between them, and was late from the people. Bilal said to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him: Shall I not establish the prayer? He said: As you wish. He established it, and the people put Abu Bakr forward. While he was praying, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, splitting the rows until he stood behind Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. They began clapping, and Abu Bakr would not turn in prayer. When they increased he turned, and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing behind him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to pray as he was. He stepped back behind, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward. When he finished he said to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him: What prevented you, when I commanded you, from having prayed? He said: It is not fitting for the son of Abu Quhafa to precede the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter of clapping in prayer? Glorification is only for men, and clapping is for women."
"5936","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached by a woman who offered herself to him, and he fell silent. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her, marry her to me? He said: Do you have anything? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you recite anything of the Qur'an? He said: Yes. He said: What? He said: Such-and-such sura and such-and-such sura. He said: I have made her yours for what you have of the Qur'an. Then I saw him go and she following him."
"5937","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Sharik al-Asadi and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, both saying: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated from Fudayl ibn Iyad from Muhammad ibn Thawr from Ma'mar from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, is Generous, loves generosity, loves lofty morals, and hates their vilest."
"5938","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Yahya ibn Ma'in from Hisham ibn Yusuf from Ma'mar from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Seventy thousand, or seven hundred thousand, of my umma shall enter Paradise without reckoning."
"5939","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Hammad ibn Salama from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Banu Amr ibn Awf over a dispute between them. The Asr prayer came, and Bilal said: Shall I establish, O Abu Bakr, and you pray with the people? Bilal established, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stepped forward and prayed with the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, piercing the rows, and the people clapped. Abu Bakr would hardly turn in his prayer; the people increased clapping, so Abu Bakr turned and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) piercing the rows. Abu Bakr stepped back, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him: Your place. He stepped back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed with the people. When he finished his prayer he said: O Abu Bakr, what is with you that when I gestured to you to remain in your place, you did not remain? He said: It was not for the son of Abu Quhafa to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said to the people: What is with you that when a matter befalls you, you clap? Glorify Allah; clapping is only for women."
"5940","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam Abu Hafs al-Tustari from Ahmad ibn Rawh al-Ahwazi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Hammad ibn Salama from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Compensate them even with a whip — meaning: in marriage."
"5941","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Nu'man; and narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Khalaf ibn Hisham; and narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Sulayman ibn Harb, all saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: There was fighting between Banu Amr ibn Awf, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He prayed Zuhr, then came to them to make peace between them, and said: O Bilal, if Asr comes and I have not come to you, order Abu Bakr to pray with the people. When Asr came he called the adhan and established, then ordered Abu Bakr, who stepped forward. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while Abu Bakr was in prayer; he split through the people until he stood behind Abu Bakr in the row next to him, and the people clapped. Abu Bakr, when he entered prayer, would not turn until he finished; when he saw the clapping not stopping he turned and saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) behind him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to continue, motioning with his hand thus. He said: Abu Bakr remained a moment, praised Allah upon the word of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then walked backwards. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he stepped forward and prayed with the people. When he finished his prayer he said: O Abu Bakr, what prevented you, when I gestured to you, from having continued? He said: It was not for the son of Abu Quhafa to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And he said to the people: If a matter confuses you, let the men glorify Allah and the women clap — and the wording is of the hadith of Arim."
"5942","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Sulayman ibn Harb; and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim, both saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah grants the servant sixty years, He has excused him and conveyed to him in age."
"5943","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim; and narrated Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani from Sulayman ibn Harb; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani, all saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and offered herself to him. He said: I have no need of women today. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, marry her to me. He said: What do you have? He said: I have nothing. He said: Give her even an iron ring. He said: I have nothing. He said: What do you have of the Qur'an? He said: Such-and-such. He said: I have made her yours for what you have of the Qur'an — and the wording is of the hadith of Arim."
"5944","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi and Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb, both saying: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated from Hammad ibn Zayd from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd that a youth of the Ansar, newly married, went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on an expedition. He returned from the road to look at his family, and there was a woman standing in the chamber. He aimed the spear at her, and she said: Enter and see what is in the house. He entered and there was a snake coiled upon his bed. He pierced it with his spear, then planted the spear in the house. The snake writhed and the man writhed; the snake died and the man died. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Muslim jinn have alighted in Medina — or he said — these houses have inhabitants; so if you see anything of them, seek refuge from it, and if it returns, kill it."
"5945","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Mubashshir ibn Mukassir from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise has a gate called al-Rayyan; those who fast are called to it. It is said to them: Come. When they have entered, that gate is closed, and none besides them enters with them."
"5946","5937 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Zayd al-Sami al-Basri from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Mubashshir ibn Mukassir from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray with their waist-wrappers knotted up around their necks because of the narrowness of the wrappers."
"5947","5938 - Narrated Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti from Muhammad ibn Aban from Mubashshir ibn Mukassir from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and offered herself to him, and he remained silent; she stood so long that we felt pity for her because of her long standing. Then a man stood up and said: Marry her to me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""What will you give her as dower?"" He said: This shawl that is on me; I have nothing besides it - he had knotted it upon his chest. The Messenger of Allah said: ""What if you use it as your garment - will you have anything besides it?"" He said: No, by Allah. He said: ""Go and seek something, even if it is an iron ring."" So he went and stayed as long as Allah willed, then came back and said: I did not find even an iron ring. He said: ""What do you have with you of the Qur'an?"" He said: Such-and-such verse and such-and-such verse. He said: ""Then I have married her to you for what you have with you of the Qur'an."""
"5948","Wuhayb ibn Khalid from Abu Hazim. 5939 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani from Ayyub ibn Yunus al-Saffar from Wuhayb from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah said: ""In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years without crossing it."""
"5949","5940 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani from Ayyub ibn Yunus from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise look upon the dwellers of the lofty chambers just as you look upon a star on the horizon of the sky."""
"5950","Yahya ibn Qays al-Kindi from Abu Hazim. 5941 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi from Hatim ibn Abbad ibn Dinar al-Harashi from Yahya ibn Qays al-Kindi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: A man from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began praising him and mentioning his worship, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. When they fell silent, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Did he remember death often?"" They said: No. He said: ""Did he abandon much of what he desired?"" They said: No. He said: ""Your companion has not attained much of what you ascribe to him."""
"5951","5942 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi from Hatim ibn Abbad ibn Dinar al-Harashi from Yahya ibn Qays al-Kindi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The intention of the believer is better than his deed, and the deed of the hypocrite is better than his intention; each acts according to his intention, and when the believer performs a deed, a light blazes in his heart."""
"5952","Yahya ibn Uthman - I think he is Basran - from Abu Hazim. 5943 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Mu'ammal ibn Ihab from al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Harashi from Ikrima ibn Ammar from Yahya ibn Uthman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You will surely follow the ways of those who came before you, handspan by handspan and cubit by cubit, until even if they entered the hole of a lizard you would follow them."" We said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews and the Christians? He said: ""Who else but the Jews and the Christians?"""
"5953","Bahr ibn Kunayz al-Saqqa' from Abu Hazim. 5944 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Hisham ibn Ammar from Ibrahim ibn A'yan from Bahr ibn Kunayz al-Saqqa' from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Heresy never appears except that denial of the divine decree comes before it."""
"5954","Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib - I think he is Basran - from Abu Hazim. 5945 - Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Ibn A'isha from Imran ibn Muhammad from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who guides to good is like the one who does it."""
"5955","Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri from Abu Hazim. 5946 - Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri - and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari, both saying - from Fudayl ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We used to pray the Friday prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would return and take the midday rest."
"5956","5947 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from al-Salt ibn Mas'ud from Fudayl ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People remain upon good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."""
"5957","5948 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from al-Salt ibn Mas'ud from Fudayl ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drink while there was a boy on his right and elders on his left; he drank and then handed it to the boy."
"5958","5949 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from al-Salt ibn Mas'ud from Fudayl ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Trench, digging while he carried the earth, and he said: ""O Allah, there is no life except the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajira."""
"5959","5950 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from al-Salt ibn Mas'ud from Fudayl ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Khaybar: ""I shall surely give the banner tomorrow to a man through whose hands Allah will grant victory."" The people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the morning, all hoping he would give them the banner. He said: ""Where is Ali?"" They said: He is complaining of his eye, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Send for him."" He was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in his eyes and supplicated, and he was healed; then he handed him the banner and said: ""Go forward and do not turn back until you come down upon the people and call them to me."" Ali went forward, then turned back: O Messenger of Allah, shall I fight them until they say there is no god but Allah? He said: ""At your ease; when you come to them, call them to the declaration that there is no god but Allah, for that a man should accept Islam at your hands is better for you than red camels."""
"5960","5951 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from al-Salt ibn Mas'ud from Fudayl ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a woman came offering herself to him; he lowered his gaze upon her and raised it, and did not send her back. A man from among his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, marry her to me. He said: ""Do you have anything?"" He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing. He said: ""Not even an iron ring?"" He said: Not even an iron ring, but I shall tear this cloak of mine and give it to her and keep half. He said: ""No; but do you have anything of the Qur'an with you?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Go, for I have married her to you for what you have with you of the Qur'an."""
"5961","5952 - With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise as it appears to people, yet he is among the people of Hell; and a man may do the deeds of the people of Hell as it appears to people, yet he is among the people of Paradise."""
"5962","5953 - With the same chain, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesture with his middle finger and the one next to the thumb: ""I have been sent, I and the Hour, like this."""
"5963","5954 - With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A morning going or an evening going in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it."""
"5964","5955 - Narrated Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hayyani from al-Hasan ibn Qaza'a from Fudayl ibn Sulayman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you laugh a laugh the like of which we never saw you laugh. He said: ""On account of a people who will be brought to Paradise in iron fetters."""
"5965","Uqba ibn Muhammad from Abu Hazim. 5956 - Narrated Musa ibn Hazim al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami from Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman from Uqba ibn Muhammad from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""With Allah, mighty and majestic, are the treasuries of good and evil; blessed is he whom He makes a key to good and a lock against evil, and woe to he whom Allah makes a key to evil and a lock against good."""
"5966","Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti from Abu Hazim. 5957 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Zayd ibn al-Huraysh from Yusuf ibn Khalid from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drink and drank from it, then handed it to a boy on his right, while the elders were on his left."
"5967","5958 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami - and narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman, both saying - from Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami, who said: I heard Abu Hazim narrating from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: There was a dispute between two quarters of the Ansar, of Banu Amr ibn Awf, until they pelted one another with stones. The cry for help reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after Bilal had called the adhan for the noon prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to make peace between them and was delayed, so Bilal came to Abu Bakr and said: Will you lead the prayer so that I may call the iqama? He said: Yes. Bilal called the iqama and Abu Bakr stepped forward; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, parting the rows until he stood behind Abu Bakr. The people began clapping, and Abu Bakr would not turn in his prayer, but when they did it much he turned, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He stepped back walking backwards, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pushed forward and prayed. When he finished the prayer he turned to Abu Bakr and said: ""What prevented you from stepping forward when I commanded you?"" He said: Allah would not let Ibn Abi Quhafa be seen leading the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer. Then he turned to the people and said: ""O people, what is with you that when something befalls you in your prayer you turn to clapping; clapping is for women and glorifying Allah is for men."""
"5968","5959 - Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm from Sahl ibn Uthman from Umar ibn Ali, who said: I heard Abu Hazim narrating from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""A morning going or an evening going in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and the space of one of your whips in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."""
"5969","5960 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Asim ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami from his father - and narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqa al-Baghdadi from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qati'i from Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami - from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever guards what is between his jaws and his thighs, Paradise is his."""
"5970","Narration of the Kufans from Abu Hazim; Sufyan al-Thawri from Abu Hazim. 5961 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar and al-Thawri from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard him narrating that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and gave herself to him, and he was silent; then she offered herself to him and he was silent. He said: I saw her standing for a long while offering herself to him while he was silent, then a man - I think from the Ansar - stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her, marry her to me. He said: ""Do you have anything?"" He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Go and seek something, even if it is an iron ring."" He went and returned, and said: By Allah, I found nothing except this garment of mine, which I shall split between me and her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no surplus in your garment beyond your need; do you recite anything of the Qur'an?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""What?"" He said: Such-and-such sura. He said: ""Then I have given her to you in marriage for what you have with you of the Qur'an."" He said: I saw him leave with her following him."
"5971","5962 - Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People remain upon good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."""
"5972","5963 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People remain upon good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."""
"5973","5964 - Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi from Qabisa - and narrated Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, both saying, from Muhammad ibn Kathir, both saying, from Sufyan - from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: They used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their waist-wrappers tied up upon their necks because of their small size, and the women were told: ""Do not raise your heads until the men sit up straight."""
"5974","5965 - Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Muhammad ibn Kathir from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We used to pray the Friday prayer, then return and take the midday rest."
"5975","5966 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father - and narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman - and narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, all saying, from Waki' from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Glorifying Allah is for men and clapping is for women."""
"5976","5967 - Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba - and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, both saying, from Waki' from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A morning going or an evening going in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it."""
"5977","5968 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Waki' from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""A morning going in the path of Allah or an evening going is better than the world and what is in it."""
"5978","5969 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas from Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat from Abu Usama from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"5979","5970 - Narrated al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya from Abu Kurayb from Mu'awiya ibn Hisham from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan, through which the fasting people enter; when they have entered it is closed."""
"5980","5970 / 2 - Narrated Abu Husayn al-Qadi from Yahya al-Himmani from Waki' from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""For every gate among the gates of righteousness there is a gate among the gates of Paradise, and the gate of fasting is called al-Rayyan."""
"5981","5971 - Narrated al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Bishri from Abu Asim from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""My pulpit stands upon a water-channel from among the water-channels of Paradise."""
"5982","5972 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Minjab al-Harith - and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam, both saying, from Khalid ibn Amr al-Umawi - from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed which, if I do it, people will love me. He said: ""Renounce the world and Allah will love you, and renounce what is in people's hands and people will love you."""
"5983","5973 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari from al-Hasan ibn Arafa from Hammad ibn al-Walid from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Everything has a purification tax, and the purification tax of the body is fasting."""
"5984","5974 - Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nayzak from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri from Sufyan al-Thawri from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never asked for anything at all but he said: No - meaning he never refused."
"5985","5975 - Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Amr ibn al-Abbas from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We used to eat the midday meal and pray the Friday prayer."
"5986","Al-Mas'udi from Abu Hazim. 5976 - Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy from Asad ibn Musa from al-Mas'udi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: There was a dispute between two men of the Ansar, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to make peace between them at prayer time. When the prayer came, Bilal came to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Abu Bakr, the prayer has come and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is not here; shall I call the adhan and the iqama while you lead? He said: As you wish. He called the adhan and the iqama, and Abu Bakr began the prayer; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came during the rest of it, and the people clapped. Abu Bakr started to step aside, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to stay in your place; when he stepped aside, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed. When he finished his prayer he said: ""O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from staying as I commanded you?"" He said: It was not for Ibn Abi Quhafa to step forward in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5987","5977 - Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali from al-Mas'udi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand leaning toward a wooden post; when the people grew numerous they said: O Messenger of Allah, the people have grown numerous - shall we not make for you a pulpit upon which you stand, for a newcomer comes and finds it hard to return without having heard anything from you? So he commanded a boy of the Ansar, who took wood from the tamarisk of the thicket and made him this pulpit. When he sat upon it, the wooden post toward which he used to stand moaned, so he came and placed his hand upon it until it fell silent."
"5988","5978 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya al-Bazzar from Isma'il ibn Umar Abu al-Mundhir al-Mas'udi from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Clapping is only for women, and glorifying Allah is for men."""
"5989","Musa ibn Muhammad al-Ansari from Abu Hazim. 5979 - Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari from Musa ibn Muhammad al-Ansari from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, a dispute has arisen among Banu Amr ibn Awf until they pelted one another with stones. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""That is old between them; rise with me to them."" Ubayy ibn Ka'b and Suhayl ibn Bayda' rose with him, and he made peace between them; the prayer came, Bilal called the adhan, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was slow in coming to them - meaning delayed. The people said to Abu Bakr: Step forward. He said: Do you think so? They said: Yes. So he stepped forward, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came; the people began clapping, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, would not turn in the prayer, but when he heard them clapping he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He stepped back on his heels, and he gestured to him: Stay in your place. He stepped back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and led the people in prayer. When he finished, he said: ""O Abu Bakr, what prevented you from staying in your place when I gestured to you?"" He said: It was not for Ibn Abi Quhafa to step forward in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Why do I see you clapping? If something befalls one in his prayer, glorifying Allah is for men and clapping is for women."""
"5990","Za'ida ibn Qudama from Abu Hazim. 5980 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Husayn ibn Ali from Za'ida from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given myself to you. He was silent, and a man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her, marry her to me. He said: ""Do you have anything?"" He said: No, by Allah. He said: ""Do you recite anything of the Qur'an?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Then I have given her to you in marriage for what you have with you of the Qur'an."""
"5991","5981 - Narrated al-Fadl ibn Abi al-Rawh al-Basri from Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban from Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi from Za'ida from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People remain upon good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."""
"5992","Al-Jarrah ibn Isa al-Asadi from Abu Hazim. 5982 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Tawwazi from Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' from al-Jarrah ibn Isa al-Asadi, Abu Muhammad, a Kufan, from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""One of you standing his ground in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it."""
"5993","Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid from Abu Hazim. 5983 - Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman - and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba - and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, all saying, from Jarir - from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: There was a dispute among the Ansar, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to them to make peace between them; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was leading the people in prayer, and he prayed behind Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"5994","Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi from Abu Hazim. 5984 - Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Suwayd ibn Sa'id from Salih ibn Musa from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd Allah ibn Amr: ""How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people, whose covenants and trusts have become mixed and who have differed, becoming like this?"" - and he interlaced his fingers. He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: ""Act upon what you recognize, leave what you disapprove of, beware of fickleness in the religion of Allah, concern yourself with your own self, and leave their common folk."""
"5995","Narration of the Egyptians from Abu Hazim; Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him. 5985 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri from Ahmad ibn Salih from Ibn Wahb from Amr ibn al-Harith from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: One of us would refrain from something even though he and she were in a single garment, fearing that something of the Qur'an would be revealed concerning it."
"5996","5986 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin and Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying, from Amr ibn Sawwad al-Sarhi from Ibn Wahb from Amr ibn al-Harith from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud wounded in his face, his front tooth broken and his helmet crushed; Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, brought him water in a shield, and Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, came and washed the blood from him, then burned a piece of mat and placed it upon his wound."
"5997","5987 - Narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri from his father, and Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rushdin from his father from his grandfather Rushdin, from Amr ibn al-Harith from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, that Abu Hazim informed him that Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi narrated to him that Adi ibn Hatim came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father used to uphold kinship, bear the burden of the weak, and feed food. He said: ""Did he reach Islam?"" He said: No. He said: ""Your father loved to be mentioned, so he has been mentioned - meaning only worldly remembrance, without reward in the Hereafter."""
"5998","Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri, originally Medinan, who settled in Alexandria, from Abu Hazim. 5988 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Sa'id ibn Mansur from Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two"" - and he pointed with his two fingers."
"5999","5989 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Sa'id ibn Mansur from Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drink while the elders were on his left and a boy, the youngest of the people, was on his right. He said to the boy: ""Will you permit me to give it to the elders?"" He said: I would not prefer anyone over my share from you. So he gave it to him."
"6000","5990 - With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had seven dinars which he placed with A'isha; when he fell ill he said: ""O A'isha, take the gold to Ali."" Then he lost consciousness, and his condition distracted A'isha, until he said that repeatedly, each time losing consciousness while his condition distracted A'isha. It was sent to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who gave it in charity. On Monday night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the throes of death, and A'isha sent her lamp to one of her womenfolk, saying: Pour for us into our lamp from your ghee-skins, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has entered the throes of death."
